COLLDATA("tadabburen","en",[[43,"§Al-Baqarah\ndeeds\nSelect three deeds that please Allah and do them, then say, \"O Allah, make me an ally of You among those You have chosen to be Your allies.\"\nExtract three etiquettes of dialogue and debate from the story of Abraham (u).\nSay, \"O Allah, the teacher of Abraham, teach me; the giver of understanding to Solomon, give me understanding.\"\nguid\nFaith and good deeds bring you closer to be an ally of Allah, while immorality and neglect of the remembrance of Allah bring you closer to be an ally of satan.\nOne of the greatest blessings of Allah upon His allies is that they are able to see with His Light.\nHaving worldly blessings without faith in Allah can be detrimental, and leads to more sinful acts.\nrefl\nٱللَّهُ وَلِيُّ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ يُخۡرِجُهُم مِّنَ ٱلظُّلُمَٰتِ إِلَى ٱلنُّورِۖ\n(Allah is the Ally of those who believe): Allah is their Defender and Helper; also, it is said that He loves them, or He is their Guardian Who never abandons them. Alhasan said: He is the guardian of their guidance. Al-Baghawi: 1/273.\nAllah is the Ally of the believers. What does that mean?\nٱللَّهُ وَلِيُّ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ يُخۡرِجُهُم مِّنَ ٱلظُّلُمَٰتِ إِلَى ٱلنُّورِۖ وَٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوٓاْ أَوۡلِيَآؤُهُمُ ٱلطَّٰغُوتُ يُخۡرِجُونَهُم مِّنَ ٱلنُّورِ إِلَى ٱلظُّلُمَٰتِۗ\nAllah mentions the light in the singular form and mentions the darkness in the plural because truth is one and disbelief is of many kinds, all of which are false. Ibn Kathir: 1/295.\nLight is mentioned in the singular form while darkness is mentioned in the plural. Why?\nٱللَّهُ وَلِيُّ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ يُخۡرِجُهُم مِّنَ ٱلظُّلُمَٰتِ إِلَى ٱلنُّورِۖ\nAllah brings them forth from the darkness of disbelief, sin and ignorance to the light of faith, obedience and knowledge. Their reward for that is that He grants them safety from the darkness of the grave, the gathering and the resurrection, and blesses them with eternal bliss, comfort, ease and joy. Al-Saadi: 111.\nWhat darkness does the believer come out of when he believes, and what light does he receive?\nٱللَّهُ وَلِيُّ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ يُخۡرِجُهُم مِّنَ ٱلظُّلُمَٰتِ إِلَى ٱلنُّورِۖ وَٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوٓاْ أَوۡلِيَآؤُهُمُ ٱلطَّٰغُوتُ يُخۡرِجُونَهُم مِّنَ ٱلنُّورِ إِلَى ٱلظُّلُمَٰتِۗ\nDisbelief is called darkness because of its obscure way, while Islam is called light due to its clear way. Al-Baghawi: 1/273.\nAllah calls disbelief darkness and calls Islam light. Why?\nٱللَّهُ وَلِيُّ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ يُخۡرِجُهُم مِّنَ ٱلظُّلُمَٰتِ إِلَى ٱلنُّورِۖ وَٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوٓاْ أَوۡلِيَآؤُهُمُ ٱلطَّٰغُوتُ يُخۡرِجُونَهُم مِّنَ ٱلنُّورِ إِلَى ٱلظُّلُمَٰتِۗ\nAllah increases the guidance of those who are guided, because following Islam makes the paths of certainty easier, so they become more deeply rooted in it with every passing day. The opposite is true for those who chose disbelief over Islam, because their choice of that indicates that their minds have been sealed, so they were not guided, and they go deeper into misguidance with every passing day. Ibn Ashur: 3/30.\nMan is bound to progress either in goodness or in evil. Explain in light of this verse.\nأَلَمۡ تَرَ إِلَى ٱلَّذِي حَآجَّ إِبۡرَٰهِۧمَ فِي رَبِّهِۦٓ\nElkiya Al-Harrasi (a religious scholar) said: This verse proves that arguing about religion is permissible. Al-Alusi: 3/19.\nIs it permissible to argue about religion?\nرَبِّيَ ٱلَّذِي يُحۡيِۦ وَيُمِيتُ\nMeaning: He is the only One Who has full control over everything. Abraham (u) specified the giving of life and causing death because they are the greatest levels of control. Al-Saadi: 111.\nAbraham singled out the giving of life and causing death for mention. Why?\nwords\nفَبُهِتَHe was overwhelmed by astonishment and could not answer\nعُرُوشِهَاIts roofs\nيَتَسَنَّهChanges\nنُنشِزُهَاRaise them and bring them together"],[44,"§Al-Baqarah\ndeeds\nGive secretly to charity today that no one knows about.\nSearch in the Quran interpretation references about the secret of ending the verses that encourage giving to charity with Allah's Attributes: All-Encompassing and Knowing.\nReach out to a person in need today, say pleasant words to him, pray for him, smile at him and give him charity, so your reward will be multiplied.\nguid\nIf spending for charity is done with love and humbleness, without reminding or hurt, it will protect the spender from fear and grief in this world and on the Day of Resurrection.\nKind words and forgiving people are better than charity that comes with reminding and hurt.\nShowing off is a sign of weak faith in Allah and the Last Day.\nrefl\nقَالَ فَخُذۡ أَرۡبَعَةٗ مِّنَ ٱلطَّيۡرِ فَصُرۡهُنَّ إِلَيۡكَ ثُمَّ ٱجۡعَلۡ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ جَبَلٖ مِّنۡهُنَّ جُزۡءٗا ثُمَّ ٱدۡعُهُنَّ يَأۡتِينَكَ سَعۡيٗاۚ وَٱعۡلَمۡ أَنَّ ٱللَّهَ عَزِيزٌ حَكِيمٞ ٢٦٠\nApparently, the wisdom behind having multiple and different kinds of birds is to further realize that bringing the dead back to life is not affected by the number of birds or their kind. Ibn Ashur: 3/39.\nWhy were the dead birds more than one, and from different kinds?\nوَٱللَّهُ يُضَٰعِفُ لِمَن يَشَآءُۚ\nThe reward will be according to the condition of the spender, his sincerity, truthfulness, and how beneficial and appropriate the spending is. Al-Saadi: 113.\nWhat makes the reward for a good deed multiply?\nٱلَّذِينَ يُنفِقُونَ أَمۡوَٰلَهُمۡ فِي سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ ثُمَّ لَا يُتۡبِعُونَ مَآ أَنفَقُواْ مَنّٗا وَلَآ أَذٗى لَّهُمۡ أَجۡرُهُمۡ عِندَ رَبِّهِمۡ وَلَا خَوۡفٌ عَلَيۡهِمۡ وَلَا هُمۡ يَحۡزَنُونَ ٢٦٢\nReminding of charity spoils its reward, and it is forbidden because only Allah reminds of His favors since all blessings come from Him. Hence, the individual must not remind others of something that came about as a result of Allah's kindness and grace, and did not come from him. Moreover, reminding another of one's favor is like enslaving him, whereas humbleness and servitude can only be to Allah. Al-Saadi: 113.\nWhy does reminding of charity spoil its reward?\nقَوۡلٞ مَّعۡرُوفٞ وَمَغۡفِرَةٌ خَيۡرٞ مِّن صَدَقَةٖ يَتۡبَعُهَآ أَذٗىۗ وَٱللَّهُ غَنِيٌّ حَلِيمٞ ٢٦٣\n(Kind words): Is to respond to one who asks for charity with pleasant words such as praying for him and saying nice words. (And forgiveness): Pardon him for any harshness. It has also been said that it is the forgiveness from Allah to you for your pleasant response. Ibn Juzay: 1/172.\nThis verse contains an example of the high moral standards in Islam. Explain.\nقَوۡلٞ مَّعۡرُوفٞ وَمَغۡفِرَةٌ خَيۡرٞ مِّن صَدَقَةٖ يَتۡبَعُهَآ أَذٗىۗ وَٱللَّهُ غَنِيٌّ حَلِيمٞ ٢٦٣\n(Most Forbearing): Allah does not hasten to punish one who disobeys Him, rather, He continues to provide him with sustenance and support while this person continues to disobey and disbelieve in Him. Al-Biqai: 1/517.\nThe verse concludes with this attribute of Allah: (Most Forbearing). Why?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ لَا تُبۡطِلُواْ صَدَقَٰتِكُم بِٱلۡمَنِّ وَٱلۡأَذَىٰ كَٱلَّذِي يُنفِقُ مَالَهُۥ رِئَآءَ ٱلنَّاسِ وَلَا يُؤۡمِنُ بِٱللَّهِ وَٱلۡيَوۡمِ ٱلۡأٓخِرِۖ\nHere is an indication that both showing off and reminding of charity are characteristics of the disbelievers, which must be avoided by the believers. Al-Alusi: 3/35.\nWhat is the difference between the charity of a sincere person and that of a person who shows off?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ لَا تُبۡطِلُواْ صَدَقَٰتِكُم بِٱلۡمَنِّ وَٱلۡأَذَىٰ\nThis proves that bad deeds nullify good deeds. Just as good deeds erase bad ones, bad deeds nullify the good deeds that came before them. Al-Saadi: 113.\nThe verse indicates the seriousness of bad deeds. Explain.\nwords\nفَصُرهُنَّ إِلَيكَHold them to you and cut them to pieces\nصَفوَانٍSmooth stone\nوَابِلٌHeavy rain\nصَلدًاBare with no dust"],[45,"§Al-Baqarah\ndeeds\nSay, \"O Allah, I ask You for steadfastness in all my affairs, the determination in following the right path and the benefit of every good deed.\"\nRemember a charity that you are hesitant about, and give it today to spite the devil.\nAsk Allah to grant you wisdom.\nguid\nBe sure to use examples, as they bring meanings closer to the mind.\nThe command to spend is a test for you, so do not spend out of inferior things to keep the good ones.\nFear of poverty is nothing but a devilish whisper; do not let poverty be a reason for you to abandon spending and doing good deeds.\nrefl\nوَمَثَلُ ٱلَّذِينَ يُنفِقُونَ أَمۡوَٰلَهُمُ ٱبۡتِغَآءَ مَرۡضَاتِ ٱللَّهِ وَتَثۡبِيتٗا مِّنۡ أَنفُسِهِمۡ\nWhoever taught himself to spend his money, which is a twin of the soul, so that his soul became submissive to him and has very little influence on him to follow its desires, then it would be easy for him to do other acts of worship. However, if he neglects restraining himself, which is imprinted with imperfections, then he will be prone to follow his desires. Al-Biqai: 1/518.\nIt is important to train oneself to spend and give. Explain in light of this verse.\nوَمَثَلُ ٱلَّذِينَ يُنفِقُونَ أَمۡوَٰلَهُمُ ٱبۡتِغَآءَ مَرۡضَاتِ ٱللَّهِ وَتَثۡبِيتٗا مِّنۡ أَنفُسِهِمۡ\nSpending is subject to two pitfalls: Either a person spends with the intention of gaining people's praise and admiration, which is showing off, or he may spend reluctantly with lack of resolve. But the people referred to in this verse are free of these two pitfalls; they spend seeking Allah's pleasure, not for any other purpose, and out of their own inner certainty. Al-Saadi: 114.\nSpending by a Muslim is subject to two pitfalls. What are they?\nوَمَثَلُ ٱلَّذِينَ يُنفِقُونَ أَمۡوَٰلَهُمُ ٱبۡتِغَآءَ مَرۡضَاتِ ٱللَّهِ وَتَثۡبِيتٗا مِّنۡ أَنفُسِهِمۡ كَمَثَلِ جَنَّةِۢ بِرَبۡوَةٍ أَصَابَهَا وَابِلٞ فَـَٔاتَتۡ أُكُلَهَا ضِعۡفَيۡنِ فَإِن لَّمۡ يُصِبۡهَا وَابِلٞ فَطَلّٞۗ\nMeaning: They give zakah willingly, with certainty of the reward and belief in Allah's promise. They know that what they give is better for them than what they keep. It was also said: They are certain that Allah will compensate them for what they spent. Al-Baghawi: 1/286.\nDescribe the state of the believer when giving zakah or charity.\nٱلشَّيۡطَٰنُ يَعِدُكُمُ ٱلۡفَقۡرَ وَيَأۡمُرُكُم بِٱلۡفَحۡشَآءِۖ\nIn this verse, satan's promise precedes his order, because through the promise a person becomes reassured. Once he feels reassured by him and fears poverty, satan will have control over him. Al-Alusi: 3/40.\nWhy is satan's promise precedes his order?\nٱلشَّيۡطَٰنُ يَعِدُكُمُ ٱلۡفَقۡرَ وَيَأۡمُرُكُم بِٱلۡفَحۡشَآءِۖ وَٱللَّهُ يَعِدُكُم مَّغۡفِرَةٗ مِّنۡهُ وَفَضۡلٗاۗ وَٱللَّهُ وَٰسِعٌ عَلِيمٞ ٢٦٨\nThe devil has a role in discouraging people from spending in the cause of Allah, and yet he commands immorality, which is sin, and spending in it. Al-Qurtubi: 4/354.\nWhat does satan do when the believer intends to give charity?\nيُؤۡتِي ٱلۡحِكۡمَةَ مَن يَشَآءُۚ وَمَن يُؤۡتَ ٱلۡحِكۡمَةَ فَقَدۡ أُوتِيَ خَيۡرٗا كَثِيرٗاۗ وَمَا يَذَّكَّرُ إِلَّآ أُوْلُواْ ٱلۡأَلۡبَٰبِ ٢٦٩\nSome wise men said : \"Whoever is given knowledge and the Quran should value himself properly and not humble himself to the people of this world for the sake of worldly enjoyment. What he has been given is better than what the people of this world have been given because Allah called this world \"Say: the enjoyment of this world is little\", and called knowledge and the Quran \"abundant good.\" Al-Qurtubi: 4/357.\nExplain the status of one who is given the Quran and knowledge?\nيُؤۡتِي ٱلۡحِكۡمَةَ مَن يَشَآءُۚ وَمَن يُؤۡتَ ٱلۡحِكۡمَةَ فَقَدۡ أُوتِيَ خَيۡرٗا كَثِيرٗاۗ\nThe soundness of the heart and the role for which it was created is to comprehend things, and not merely knowing them. One may know something without comprehension. In fact, he can be oblivious to it and neglectful of it. The one who comprehends something begins with writing it down, grasping it, becoming fully aware of it and keeping it in his heart to gain self-sufficiency during the time of need. It is only then that his deeds will match his words, and his inside will coincide with his outside; and that is the one who has been given wisdom. Ibn Taimyah: 599.\nWhat is the sign of reason and wisdom?\nwords\nبِرَبوَةٍAt a high ground\nفَطَلٌّA drizzle\nتَيَمَّمُواAim toward\nتُغمِضُواOverlooking its defects"],[46,"§Al-Baqarah\ndeeds\nIdentify some people who are heedless, and ask Allah persistently to guide them so that Allah may reward you for it.\nRecall a past sin of yours, then give to charity so that Allah may forgive you.\nLook for a charitable cause that people have been slow to donate to, and take the initiative and announce your charity so that you will receive the reward of people following your example.\nguid\nConcealing or disclosing good deeds differ according to the benefit sought from each of them.\nThe preacher to Allah should focus on the proper conveying of his message; he is not required to have people respond to his call.\nAccustom yourself to be content with what you have, and refrain from asking people for anything, as whoever is content with what Allah has given him, Allah will make him self-sufficient.\nrefl\nوَمَآ أَنفَقۡتُم مِّن نَّفَقَةٍ أَوۡ نَذَرۡتُم مِّن نَّذۡرٖ فَإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ يَعۡلَمُهُۥۗ وَمَا لِلظَّٰلِمِينَ مِنۡ أَنصَارٍ ٢٧٠\nAllah will come to the aid of a generous man whenever he stumbles, while the wrongdoer who transgressed rather than doing good will have no help from Allah. Al-Biqai: 1/525.\nAfter urging the believers to give to charity, the verse concludes with: (But the wrongdoers have no helpers). Why?\nإِن تُبۡدُواْ ٱلصَّدَقَٰتِ فَنِعِمَّا هِيَۖ وَإِن تُخۡفُوهَا وَتُؤۡتُوهَا ٱلۡفُقَرَآءَ فَهُوَ خَيۡرٞ لَّكُمۡۚ\nThis indicates that charity given secretly to the poor is better than charity given openly, but if charity is not being given to the poor, then the verse implies that giving secretly is not better than that which is given openly. It depends on what serves a greater purpose. If giving charity openly makes acts of worship visible, and encourages others to follow, then it is better than doing it in private. Al-Saadi: 116.\nWhen giving charity, which is better: doing it publicly or privately?\nوَإِن تُخۡفُوهَا وَتُؤۡتُوهَا ٱلۡفُقَرَآءَ فَهُوَ خَيۡرٞ لَّكُمۡۚ\nThis indicates that concealing charity is better than disclosing it because it is further from showing off. Ibn Kathir: 1/305.\nWhy is concealing charity is better than disclosing it?\nوَمَا تُنفِقُونَ إِلَّا ٱبۡتِغَآءَ وَجۡهِ ٱللَّهِۚ\nSpend only for the sake of Allah without causing hurt, reminding others of it, showing off nor spending out of inferior things. Al-Alusi: 3/46.\nList some of the pitfalls that nullify the charities or reduce their reward?\nلِلۡفُقَرَآءِ ٱلَّذِينَ أُحۡصِرُواْ فِي سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ لَا يَسۡتَطِيعُونَ ضَرۡبٗا فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ يَحۡسَبُهُمُ ٱلۡجَاهِلُ أَغۡنِيَآءَ مِنَ ٱلتَّعَفُّفِ تَعۡرِفُهُم بِسِيمَٰهُمۡ لَا يَسۡٔلُونَ ٱلنَّاسَ إِلۡحَافٗاۗ وَمَا تُنفِقُواْ مِنۡ خَيۡرٖ فَإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ بِهِۦ عَلِيمٌ ٢٧٣\nAn ignorant person would think they were self-sufficient because they were not asking others. (Restraint) is refrainment from requesting. (You will know them by their sign): Their faces show tiredness, destitution and lack of blessings. It was also said: Humbleness or prostration marks. (They do not ask people persistently): They ask people graciously or they never ask at all. Ibn Juzay: 1/127.\nWhat are the qualities for which Allah praised the poor believers in this verse?\nلِلۡفُقَرَآءِ ٱلَّذِينَ أُحۡصِرُواْ فِي سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ لَا يَسۡتَطِيعُونَ ضَرۡبٗا فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ يَحۡسَبُهُمُ ٱلۡجَاهِلُ أَغۡنِيَآءَ مِنَ ٱلتَّعَفُّفِ\nThe poor immigrants (Muhajireen) are singled out because they were the only poor people at that time. They were the people of the Suffah (verandah), and they about four hundred men. That was because the poor used to come to the Messenger of Allah (r), and they had neither family nor property and so a verandah (Suffah) was built for them in the mosque of the Messenger of Allah (r), which is why they were called the People of the Suffah. Al-Qurtubi: 4/371.\nWhy were the people of \"Suffah\" poor?\nٱلَّذِينَ يُنفِقُونَ أَمۡوَٰلَهُم بِٱلَّيۡلِ وَٱلنَّهَارِ سِرّٗا وَعَلَانِيَةٗ فَلَهُمۡ أَجۡرُهُمۡ عِندَ رَبِّهِمۡ وَلَا خَوۡفٌ عَلَيۡهِمۡ وَلَا هُمۡ يَحۡزَنُونَ ٢٧٤\nThe (night) is mentioned before (day) and (secret) is before (public), to indicate the advantage of concealment over disclosure. Al-Alusi: 3/47.\nWhy is (night) mentioned before (day), and (secret) before (public)?\nwords\nأُحصِرُواThose who have been restricted for the cause of Allah, unable to move about in the land for sustenance\nبِسِيمَاهُمTheir characteristic signs\nإِلحَافًاAsking persistently"],[47,"§Al-Baqarah\ndeeds\nShare a message warning of the risk of usury to those who deal with it and to Muslims.\nMaintain the five daily prayers in congregation.\nHelp an insolvent person, or intercede for him to pay his debt.\nguid\nHe who deals in usury has lost the wisdom that leads him to the path of truth.\nUnlawfully earned money is devoid of blessings and harmful to its owner, while giving to charity leads to happiness in this life and the Hereafter.\nThis verse needs to be repeated so that its meaning settles in the heart, and its effect flows to the rest of the body.\nrefl\nٱلَّذِينَ يَأۡكُلُونَ ٱلرِّبَوٰاْ لَا يَقُومُونَ إِلَّا كَمَا يَقُومُ ٱلَّذِي يَتَخَبَّطُهُ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنُ مِنَ ٱلۡمَسِّۚ\nHe will be resurrected like a madman as a punishment to him and to make him hated by all those who will be gathered on the Last Day. Al-Qurtubi: 4/390.\nHow will the consumer of usury going to be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection?\nيَمۡحَقُ ٱللَّهُ ٱلرِّبَوٰاْ وَيُرۡبِي ٱلصَّدَقَٰتِۗ وَٱللَّهُ لَا يُحِبُّ كُلَّ كَفَّارٍ أَثِيمٍ ٢٧٦\nThere is a reason for concluding this verse with this description, which that the usurer is not satisfied with what Allah has allotted him of lawful earnings, nor is he content with what He has prescribed for him of permissible earnings. He strives to consume people's wealth through various types of wicked earnings. He is ungrateful for the blessings bestowed upon him, unjust and sinful, and consumes people's wealth unjustly. Ibn Kathir: 1/312.\nWhy is the usurer described as a sinning disbeliever?\nيَمۡحَقُ ٱللَّهُ ٱلرِّبَوٰاْ وَيُرۡبِي ٱلصَّدَقَٰتِۗ وَٱللَّهُ لَا يُحِبُّ كُلَّ كَفَّارٍ أَثِيمٍ ٢٧٦\nIbn Abbas (t) said: (Allah destroys usury) means that Allah does not accept charity, Jihad or Hajj from a usurer. (And nourishes charities) means that Allah increases and blesses them in this life and multiplies their reward in the Hereafter. (Allah does not like every sinning disbeliever) who does not believe in prohibiting usury. (Sinning) who consumes it. Al-Baghawi: 1/302.\nWhat is the effect of usury on those who consume it?\nيَمۡحَقُ ٱللَّهُ ٱلرِّبَوٰاْ وَيُرۡبِي ٱلصَّدَقَٰتِۗ\nThat is because the requital befits the action. The usurer has wronged people and taken their wealth in an unlawful manner will be punished by losing his wealth. The one who does good to them with various types of goodness will be rewarded by his Lord, who is more generous than him, so Allah will do good to him as he did good to His servants. Al-Saadi: 117.\nWhy is the reward of the usurer the loss of his wealth, and the reward of the doer of good is the increase of his good deeds?\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ وَعَمِلُواْ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ وَأَقَامُواْ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ وَءَاتَوُاْ ٱلزَّكَوٰةَ لَهُمۡ أَجۡرُهُمۡ عِندَ رَبِّهِمۡ وَلَا خَوۡفٌ عَلَيۡهِمۡ وَلَا هُمۡ يَحۡزَنُونَ ٢٧٧\nHere, Allah specifies prayer and zakah, even though they are included in the righteous deeds, to honor them and draw attention to their importance, as they are the most important of deeds: Prayer is the highest action of the body, and zakah is highest action in wealth management. Al-Qurtubi: 4/403.\nAllah singles out prayer and zakah for mention. Why?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ ٱتَّقُواْ ٱللَّهَ وَذَرُواْ مَا بَقِيَ مِنَ ٱلرِّبَوٰٓاْ إِن كُنتُم مُّؤۡمِنِينَ ٢٧٨\nUsury and faith cannot coexist. Most of the calamities that befell this nation (Muslims) are due to those who practice usury until they were hit by extreme hardship and drought, similar to what had befallen the Children of Israel before them. Al-Biqai: 1/541.\nWhy is the prohibition of usury emphasized?\nوَٱتَّقُواْ يَوۡمٗا تُرۡجَعُونَ فِيهِ إِلَى ٱللَّهِۖ ثُمَّ تُوَفَّىٰ كُلُّ نَفۡسٖ مَّا كَسَبَتۡ وَهُمۡ لَا يُظۡلَمُونَ ٢٨١\nIf a person knows that he will return to Allah and that He will requite him for all his deeds, great and small, public and private, and that Allah will not wrong him in the slightest way, this will necessitate hope for Allah's reward and fear of His punishment. Al-Saadi: 117-118.\nWhat will be the result for a person when he knows that he will return to Allah?\nwords\nيَتَخَبَّطُهُBeaten\nالمَسِّInsanity\nيَمحَقُDestroys\nوَيُربِيIncreases and nourishes\nفَأذَنُواBe certain"],[48,"§Al-Baqarah\ndeeds\nStart today by documenting all debts (due to you or to others) in order to preserve your rights, the rights of your heirs, and the rights of others.\nLend money to a person who is in need and write it down.\nIdentify a skill given to you by Allah and teach it to others as a show of gratitude to Him.\nguid\nControlling financial dealings is a way to controlling heart deeds, which leads to the good of faith and life.\nIt is incumbent upon anyone who has been bestowed with a blessing that people need, to share it with them as a show of gratitude to Him.\nFear of Allah is the first step toward achieving knowledge.\nrefl\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوٓاْ إِذَا تَدَايَنتُم بِدَيۡنٍ إِلَىٰٓ أَجَلٖ مُّسَمّٗى فَٱكۡتُبُوهُۚ\nAllah commands documenting debts to preserve financial rights and safeguard against doubt. If the debtor is righteous, then writing debt will not harm him. Al-Qurtubi: 4/431.\nAllah commands documenting debts and similar transactions. Why?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوٓاْ إِذَا تَدَايَنتُم بِدَيۡنٍ إِلَىٰٓ أَجَلٖ مُّسَمّٗى فَٱكۡتُبُوهُۚ\nIt is ordained to put in writing all contracts that are based on credit. It is necessary to do so because without documentation there is a great risk of problems such as mistakes, forgetfulness, disputes, and quarrels, which are serious problems. Al-Saadi: 118.\nIslamic Sharia mandates writing down debts. Why?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوٓاْ إِذَا تَدَايَنتُم بِدَيۡنٍ إِلَىٰٓ أَجَلٖ مُّسَمّٗى فَٱكۡتُبُوهُۚ\nContracting debts is one of the biggest business stimulators because an entrepreneur may need to borrow money in order to start a good and profitable business in trade, industry or agriculture. A rich person who spends his money lavishly may run out of money if he does not have continuous returns through lending to investors, otherwise, his wealth will be wiped out. Ibn Ashur: 3/98.\nWhat is the wisdom behind allowing contracting debts in Islamic Sharia?\nوَلۡيَكۡتُب بَّيۡنَكُمۡ كَاتِبُۢ بِٱلۡعَدۡلِۚ\nThe scribe must be knowledgeable about writing documents, what each party is required to do, and how to obtain authentication, because justice can only be achieved through this. Al-Saadi: 118.\nWho is a good scribe for writing debts?\nفَإِن لَّمۡ يَكُونَا رَجُلَيۡنِ فَرَجُلٞ وَٱمۡرَأَتَانِ مِمَّن تَرۡضَوۡنَ مِنَ ٱلشُّهَدَآءِ\nUprightness of the witness is a condition where he is known for refraining from major sins and not persistent on minor ones. Noble sense of the witness is a condition, which is related to the morals of the soul, where he is known to have a good appearance and conduct, and stable profession. If he displays unbecoming practices in public, then he lacks enough noble sense and his testimony is rejected. Al-Baghawi: 1/309.\nWhat is meant by noble sense and uprightness?\nوَٱتَّقُواْ ٱللَّهَۖ وَيُعَلِّمُكُمُ ٱللَّهُۗ وَٱللَّهُ بِكُلِّ شَيۡءٍ عَلِيمٞ ٢٨٢\nThis is a promise from Allah that He will teach whoever fears Him, that is, He will enlighten his heart so that he understands what is conveyed to him, and will grant him a criterion by which he will distinguish between truth and falsehood. Al-Qurtubi: 4/464.\nHow does a servant gain knowledge from Allah, the Almighty?\nوَٱتَّقُواْ ٱللَّهَۖ وَيُعَلِّمُكُمُ ٱللَّهُۗ وَٱللَّهُ بِكُلِّ شَيۡءٍ عَلِيمٞ ٢٨٢\nThese verses of transactions are concluded with Allah's attribute of knowledge after the command to fear Him, which is very appropriate for the tricks that those who deal with them use to bring good fortune to themselves. Moreover, it encourages them to comply with what they have been commanded to do. Al-Biqai: 1/549.\nWhy are these verses of transactions conclude by mentioning Allah's attribute of Knowledge after the command to fear Him?\nwords\nو لا یأبَShould not refuse\nوَليُملِلِLet him dictate and acknowledge\nيَبخَسReduces\nسَفِيهًاFeeble-minded / legally incompetent\nضَعِيفًاWeak due to young age or insanity\nتَسأَمُواDo not be weary\nوَأَقوَمُ لِلشَّهَادَةِIt is equitable in the sight of Allah, and more supportive as evidence"],[49,"§Al-Baqarah\ndeeds\nRecite the two verses at the end of Surat Al-Baqarah at night, for they are sufficient for whoever recites them.\nBe sure today, after you finish any act of obedience or good deed, to ask Allah Almighty for forgiveness.\nDo a good deed today with your words, wealth, or your limbs, then supplicate Allah, for it is more likely that your supplication will be answered.\nguid\nA person who conceals testimony is sinful in heart, let alone a person who lies in testimony, so how about one who lies in his testimony?\nHearing and obeying Allah's commands are means to attain His forgiveness, glory be to Him.\nAllegiance to Allah, the Almighty, is a cause for victory over enemies.\nrefl\nفَلۡيُؤَدِّ ٱلَّذِي ٱؤۡتُمِنَ أَمَٰنَتَهُۥ وَلۡيَتَّقِ ٱللَّهَ رَبَّهُۥۗ\nAllah commands fearing Him when paying back the debt as well as when acknowledging its receipt, in order to honor the rights of people and warn against what causes corruption. Al-Alusi: 3/63.\nAllah commands fearing Him upon fulfillment and again upon acknowledgment. Why?\nوَمَن يَكۡتُمۡهَا فَإِنَّهُۥٓ ءَاثِمٞ قَلۡبُهُۥۗ وَٱللَّهُ بِمَا تَعۡمَلُونَ عَلِيمٞ ٢٨٣\nThe heart is described as (sinful) because concealment is a deed of the heart. The heart is a lump of flesh that when it is sound, the whole body becomes sound. Al-Qurtubi: 4/478.\nWhy is heart described as (sinful)?\nوَإِن كُنتُمۡ عَلَىٰ سَفَرٖ وَلَمۡ تَجِدُواْ كَاتِبٗا فَرِهَٰنٞ مَّقۡبُوضَةٞۖ فَإِنۡ أَمِنَ بَعۡضُكُم بَعۡضٗا فَلۡيُؤَدِّ ٱلَّذِي ٱؤۡتُمِنَ أَمَٰنَتَهُۥ وَلۡيَتَّقِ ٱللَّهَ رَبَّهُۥۗ وَلَا تَكۡتُمُواْ ٱلشَّهَٰدَةَۚ وَمَن يَكۡتُمۡهَا فَإِنَّهُۥٓ ءَاثِمٞ قَلۡبُهُۥۗ وَٱللَّهُ بِمَا تَعۡمَلُونَ عَلِيمٞ ٢٨٣\nThese good rulings to which Allah has guided his servants, include great wisdom and serve great purposes, indicating that if people followed Allah's guidance, their worldly and spiritual affairs would be sound, as these rulings include justice and that which is in their best interests; their rights would be protected, quarrels and conflicts would be prevented, and people's livelihood would be satisfactory. Al-Saadi: 119-120.\nWhat makes people affairs, both worldly and spiritual, sound?\nوَقَالُواْ سَمِعۡنَا وَأَطَعۡنَاۖ غُفۡرَانَكَ رَبَّنَا وَإِلَيۡكَ ٱلۡمَصِيرُ ٢٨٥\nGiving priority to hearing and obedience over asking for forgiveness is giving priority to the means over the request, and that makes the supplication more likely to be accepted and answered by Allah. Al-Alusi: 3/69.\nHearing and obeying are mentioned before requesting forgiveness. Why?\nلَا يُكَلِّفُ ٱللَّهُ نَفۡسًا إِلَّا وُسۡعَهَاۚ\nIn principle, the commands and prohibitions are not too difficult for people to adhere to; rather, they are nourishment for the soul, remedy for the body, and protection from harm. Allah commanded the servants what He commanded them out of mercy and kindness. Al-Saadi: 120.\nSharia's laws and teachings are mercy and kindness from Allah. Explain in light of this verse.\nلَا يُكَلِّفُ ٱللَّهُ نَفۡسًا إِلَّا وُسۡعَهَاۚ لَهَا مَا كَسَبَتۡ وَعَلَيۡهَا مَا ٱكۡتَسَبَتۡۗ\n(For it), this expression is used for good deeds because a person rejoices in earning them and are added to his possession. (Against it), this is used for bad deeds because they are like burdens and sins and hard to bear. This is like saying: \"I have wealth\" and \"I owe a debt.\" Al-Qurtubi: 4/500.\nExplain the use of these words: (for it) and (against it).\nوَٱعۡفُ عَنَّا وَٱغۡفِرۡ لَنَا وَٱرۡحَمۡنَآۚ\n(Pardon us), for whatever between us and You of what You know of our shortcomings and misdeeds. (And grant us forgiveness), for whatever between us and Your servants, thus, do not expose our sins and evil deeds to them. (And have mercy upon us), do not let us fall into another sin. It is said that a sinner needs three things: Allah's forgiveness for what is between him and Allah, that Allah conceals his sins from His servants, thus He does not disgrace him among them, and that Allah protects him so that he does not fall into the same. Ibn Kathir: 1/324.\nA sinner needs three things. What are they?\nwords\nفَرِهَانٌ مَقبُوضَةٌSomething should be taken by the creditor as collateral until the debtor pays back the debt\nإِصرًاA burden and hardship"],[50,"§Al-Imran\ndeeds\nMake a plan to study and reflect on the meanings of Surat Al-Imran, for it will come pleading for you on the Day of Resurrection.\nSay this repeatedly, today, \"O My Lord, increase my knowledge.\"\nAsk Allah repeatedly, today, to help you stay steadfast in guidance and truth.\nguid\nIf one plans to commit a sin, can he find a hidden place from Allah?\nYour physical appearance and looks are all from Allah, so be content with what Allah has given you.\nKnow that abandoning clear evidence and citing unspecific terms is the path of those who have deviant hearts.\nrefl\nنَزَّلَ عَلَيۡكَ ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ بِٱلۡحَقِّ مُصَدِّقٗا لِّمَا بَيۡنَ يَدَيۡهِ وَأَنزَلَ ٱلتَّوۡرَىٰةَ وَٱلۡإِنجِيلَ ٣\nAllah says, (And revealed the Torah and the Gospel) because each one was sent down as one whole, while He says about the Quran (He has sent down to you the Book) because it was sent down in portions. Al-Baghawi: 1/320.\nAllah Says about the Torah and Gospel (revealed), and says about the Quran (sent down). Why?\nمُصَدِّقٗا لِّمَا بَيۡنَ يَدَيۡهِ\n(Confirming what came before it) of the previous books. So, it is a judge over them; what it confirms is to be accepted and what it refutes is to be rejected. The Quran is consistent with them in all the requirements agreed upon by the messengers. These books testify that the Quran is truly from Allah. If the People of the Book do not believe in the Quran, then they cannot truly believe in their books; their disbelief in the Quran invalidates their belief in their books. Al-Saadi: 121.\nThis verse indicates that the Quran is a criterion over other revealed books. How?\nهُوَ ٱلَّذِيٓ أَنزَلَ عَلَيۡكَ ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ مِنۡهُ ءَايَٰتٞ مُّحۡكَمَٰتٌ هُنَّ أُمُّ ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ وَأُخَرُ مُتَشَٰبِهَٰتٞۖ\nAllah sent down verses that are unspecific to distinguish the scholars who are keen to study and reflect on their meanings to gain the knowledge in order to infer the true aims behind Sharia's laws and teachings. By doing that, they may attain the high ranks by exhausting their minds and extracting the sublime purposes and appropriate meanings. Al-Alusi: 3/83.\nWhat is the wisdom behind sending down verses that are unspecific?\nفَأَمَّا ٱلَّذِينَ فِي قُلُوبِهِمۡ زَيۡغٞ فَيَتَّبِعُونَ مَا تَشَٰبَهَ مِنۡهُ ٱبۡتِغَآءَ ٱلۡفِتۡنَةِ\n(Those with deviant hearts), those who are misguided and deviate from truth to falsehood. (Follow that which is unspecific), so that they can distort its meanings to suit their corrupt purposes because its wording may be interpreted in accordance with what they intend. As for the definite verses, they cannot be distorted because they are clear, thus, constitute unequivocal proof against misguided people. For this reason, Allah the Most High says, (Seeking discord), to mislead their followers by pretending to prove their innovations by relying on the Quran, while, in fact, it is an argument against them, not for them. Ibn Kathir: 1/336.\nWhat is the attitude of innovators toward the unspecific verses of the Quran?\nفَأَمَّا ٱلَّذِينَ فِي قُلُوبِهِمۡ زَيۡغٞ فَيَتَّبِعُونَ مَا تَشَٰبَهَ مِنۡهُ ٱبۡتِغَآءَ ٱلۡفِتۡنَةِ وَٱبۡتِغَآءَ تَأۡوِيلِهِۦۖ\nAllah makes it clear that no one will be misguided by the unspecific verses except those with a crooked nature who are not firmly rooted in religion and whose knowledge is not enlightened in science. Al-Biqai: 2/22.\nWho is likely to be misguided by the unspecific verses of the Quran?\nوَٱلرَّٰسِخُونَ فِي ٱلۡعِلۡمِ يَقُولُونَ ءَامَنَّا بِهِۦ كُلّٞ مِّنۡ عِندِ رَبِّنَاۗ وَمَا يَذَّكَّرُ إِلَّآ أُوْلُواْ ٱلۡأَلۡبَٰبِ ٧\nThis is a praise to those who are well grounded in the quality of their minds and good insight, because their minds have been stripped of what clouds them of reliance on false desires, and they have prepared themselves to be guided to the landmarks of truth and to ascend to the heights of rightness. Al-Alusi: 3/83.\nWhat is the significance of the Almighty's saying: (None will take heed except people of understanding)?\nرَبَّنَا لَا تُزِغۡ قُلُوبَنَا بَعۡدَ إِذۡ هَدَيۡتَنَا وَهَبۡ لَنَا مِن لَّدُنكَ رَحۡمَةًۚ إِنَّكَ أَنتَ ٱلۡوَهَّابُ ٨\nAllah's general mercy encompasses all of His creations, the good and bad, the believers and disbelievers. Then He has mercy given to the believers in particular, which is the mercy of faith. Then, He has mercy given to the righteous only, which is the mercy of obedience to Allah, the Most High. Moreover, He has mercy given to His allies only, by which they attained higher rank with Him. Furthermore, He has mercy given to His Prophets only, by which they attained Prophethood. Those who are well-grounded in knowledge supplicate Allah by saying: (and grant us Your Mercy). Ibn Taimyah: 2/34.\nList some types of Allah's Mercy toward His creation?\nwords\nالقَيُّومُThe All-Sustaining\nمُحكَمَاتٌPrecise and definite\nأُمُّ الكِتَابِFoundation of the Book\nمُتَشَابِهَاتٌUnspecific\nزَيغٌDeviation\nتَأوِيلِهِTrue interpretation"],[51,"§Al-Imran\ndeeds\nRecall a major sin that you committed in the past, and hasten to ask for Allah's forgiveness.\nShare a message in which you remind others that at the end, the battle will be won by those who fear Allah.\nWhile enjoying worldly pleasures, ask Allah to keep your heart safe from being attached to them.\nguid\nKeep busy doing good deeds because they are the grounds for entering Paradise, not the abundance of wealth and children, so focus on what benefits you.\nSins are the path to punishment in this life and the Hereafter.\nOne of the best ways to confront temptations and desires is to remember the Hereafter and Allah's promise for those who abstain from them.\nrefl\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ لَن تُغۡنِيَ عَنۡهُمۡ أَمۡوَٰلُهُمۡ وَلَآ أَوۡلَٰدُهُم مِّنَ ٱللَّهِ شَيۡٔاۖ وَأُوْلَٰٓئِكَ هُمۡ وَقُودُ ٱلنَّارِ ١٠\nThese disbelievers have been fully distracted by their wealth and children from the way of Allah and what ought to be done for the Hereafter, to the point where it seems to the observer that they are among those who believe that their wealth and children will replace the mercy of Allah Almighty and His obedience. Al-Alusi: 3/93.\nAllah makes clear that neither the wealth of the disbelievers nor their children will avail them. Why?\nوَٱللَّهُ يُؤَيِّدُ بِنَصۡرِهِۦ مَن يَشَآءُۚ إِنَّ فِي ذَٰلِكَ لَعِبۡرَةٗ لِّأُوْلِي ٱلۡأَبۡصَٰرِ ١٣\nMeaning: Victory is by the will of Allah, not by numbers, as Muslims defeated the disbelievers even though they were outnumbered. Ibn Juzay: 1/138.\nIs maintaining powerful arms and large army a true criterion for victory? Explain.\nوَٱللَّهُ يُؤَيِّدُ بِنَصۡرِهِۦ مَن يَشَآءُۚ إِنَّ فِي ذَٰلِكَ لَعِبۡرَةٗ لِّأُوْلِي ٱلۡأَبۡصَٰرِ ١٣\nIf one looks at the mere apparent causes, numbers, and equipment of both sides, he will be certain that it is impossible for this small group to prevail over that large group. But behind this cause that is visible to the eyes is a greater cause that is only perceived by people of insight, faith in Allah, reliance on Him, and trust in His sufficiency, which is His victory and honor for His believing servants over His disbelieving enemies. Al-Saadi: 123.\nThis verse ends with: (Indeed in that is a lesson for those who have insight), why?\nزُيِّنَ لِلنَّاسِ حُبُّ ٱلشَّهَوَٰتِ مِنَ ٱلنِّسَآءِ وَٱلۡبَنِينَ وَٱلۡقَنَٰطِيرِ ٱلۡمُقَنطَرَةِ مِنَ ٱلذَّهَبِ وَٱلۡفِضَّةِ وَٱلۡخَيۡلِ ٱلۡمُسَوَّمَةِ وَٱلۡأَنۡعَٰمِ وَٱلۡحَرۡثِۗ ذَٰلِكَ مَتَٰعُ ٱلۡحَيَوٰةِ ٱلدُّنۡيَاۖ وَٱللَّهُ عِندَهُۥ حُسۡنُ ٱلۡمَٔابِ ١٤\nThe point of this analogy is that paradise can only be attained by abandoning desires and weaning the soul from them . Al-Qurtubi: 5/43.\nWhat is the link between mentioning desires and the best return?\nزُيِّنَ لِلنَّاسِ حُبُّ ٱلشَّهَوَٰتِ مِنَ ٱلنِّسَآءِ وَٱلۡبَنِينَ وَٱلۡقَنَٰطِيرِ ٱلۡمُقَنطَرَةِ\nAllah starts with women, because the temptation caused by them is more severe, as the Messenger (r) said: \"I have not left behind me any temptation more harmful to men than women.\" However, if the intention is to have children and preserve one's chastity, then it is desirable and recommended. Ibn Kathir: 1/332.\nThis verse starts with women in the types of desires. Why?\nزُيِّنَ لِلنَّاسِ حُبُّ ٱلشَّهَوَٰتِ مِنَ ٱلنِّسَآءِ وَٱلۡبَنِينَ وَٱلۡقَنَٰطِيرِ ٱلۡمُقَنطَرَةِ مِنَ ٱلذَّهَبِ وَٱلۡفِضَّةِ وَٱلۡخَيۡلِ ٱلۡمُسَوَّمَةِ وَٱلۡأَنۡعَٰمِ وَٱلۡحَرۡثِۗ ذَٰلِكَ مَتَٰعُ ٱلۡحَيَوٰةِ ٱلدُّنۡيَاۖ\nThese particular desires are singled out for mention because they are the greatest pleasures in this world, and others are secondary to them. Al-Saadi: 124.\nThese particular desires are singled out for mention. Why?\nقُلۡ أَؤُنَبِّئُكُم بِخَيۡرٖ مِّن ذَٰلِكُمۡۖ لِلَّذِينَ ٱتَّقَوۡاْ عِندَ رَبِّهِمۡ جَنَّٰتٞ تَجۡرِي مِن تَحۡتِهَا ٱلۡأَنۡهَٰرُ خَٰلِدِينَ فِيهَا وَأَزۡوَٰجٞ مُّطَهَّرَةٞ وَرِضۡوَٰنٞ مِّنَ ٱللَّهِۗ\nIn this verse, Allah starts by mentioning the abode, which is the gardens of Paradise. Secondly; He mentions what brings about complete intimacy, which is the purified spouses. Thirdly; He mentions the greatest elixir and the spirit for the heart of the devotee, which is the pleasure of Allah. Al-Alusi: 3/101.\nWhat is Allah's reward for the righteous in the Hereafter?\nwords\nكَدَأبِLike the habitual way\nوَالقَنَاطِيرِ المُقَنطَرَةِAbundance of gold and silver\nالمُسَوَّمَةِFine branded horses\nوَالحَرثِWell-tilled land\nالمَآبِPlace of return"],[52,"§Al-Imran\ndeeds\nLeave out something you love for a day in order to discipline yourself.\nSupplicate Allah for something you want, but make a good deed before that, so that your supplication is more likely to be answered.\nPray at night, even if it is a few rak'as, and then ask for Allah's forgiveness.\nguid\nHumble yourself to Allah because no matter how high you think you have reached in servitude to Him, you will always come short.\nThe knowledge of Tawhīd is the most important subject matter in Sharia teachings, hence, so be sure to have a broad knowledge of it.\nIt was not lack of knowledge that caused destruction of the people of the Scripture, rather it was using their knowledge to commit transgression among themselves due to envy.\nrefl\nٱلصَّٰبِرِينَ وَٱلصَّٰدِقِينَ وَٱلۡقَٰنِتِينَ وَٱلۡمُنفِقِينَ وَٱلۡمُسۡتَغۡفِرِينَ بِٱلۡأَسۡحَارِ ١٧\nDedicating the pre-dawn hours to seeking Allah's forgiveness is because supplication during these times is more likely to be answered, as worship is more difficult, the soul is purer, and the heart is more attentive. Al-Alusi: 3/102.\nWhy was the pre-dawn time selected for asking for Allah's forgiveness?\nٱلصَّٰبِرِينَ وَٱلصَّٰدِقِينَ وَٱلۡقَٰنِتِينَ وَٱلۡمُنفِقِينَ وَٱلۡمُسۡتَغۡفِرِينَ بِٱلۡأَسۡحَارِ ١٧\nThey used to spend the night in prayer, then before dawn, they used to sit and ask for Allah's forgiveness, thus, concluding their night prayers with seeking forgiveness. Ibn Taimyah: 2/39.\nWhat do most worshiping acts conclude with?\nشَهِدَ ٱللَّهُ أَنَّهُۥ لَآ إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا هُوَ وَٱلۡمَلَٰٓئِكَةُ وَأُوْلُواْ ٱلۡعِلۡمِ قَآئِمَۢا بِٱلۡقِسۡطِۚ لَآ إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا هُوَ ٱلۡعَزِيزُ ٱلۡحَكِيمُ ١٨\nThis proves that the noblest of matters is knowledge of Tawhīd (Oneness of Allah), because Allah Himself testified to it, and the best of His creation testified to it. Testimony can only be based on knowledge and certainty, like witnessing with the eyes. Al-Saadi: 125.\nWhat is the status of the knowledge of Tawhīd? How can you infer that from this verse?\nشَهِدَ ٱللَّهُ أَنَّهُۥ لَآ إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا هُوَ وَٱلۡمَلَٰٓئِكَةُ وَأُوْلُواْ ٱلۡعِلۡمِ قَآئِمَۢا بِٱلۡقِسۡطِۚ لَآ إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا هُوَ ٱلۡعَزِيزُ ٱلۡحَكِيمُ ١٨\nThis verse highlights the importance of knowledge in many ways such as Allah mentions the testimony of scholars alongside His Own and that of His angels, which is a sufficient honor. He made them witnesses and an argument against people, and obligated the people to act in accordance with the witnessed matter. Thus, Allah obligated people to adhere to the belief in His Oneness, so whoever follows that, the scholars will get part of the reward for it. This is the bounty of Allah that He bestows upon whomever He wills. The fact that He includes the people of knowledge among the witnesses implies that they are praiseworthy and of good character, and that they are trustworthy and able to take care of what He entrusted to them. Al-Saadi: 125.\nThe verse indicates the honor of knowledge and scholars in several ways. Explain.\nإِنَّ ٱلدِّينَ عِندَ ٱللَّهِ ٱلۡإِسۡلَٰمُۗ وَمَا ٱخۡتَلَفَ ٱلَّذِينَ أُوتُواْ ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ إِلَّا مِنۢ بَعۡدِ مَا جَآءَهُمُ ٱلۡعِلۡمُ بَغۡيَۢا بَيۡنَهُمۡۗ وَمَن يَكۡفُرۡ بِـَٔايَٰتِ ٱللَّهِ فَإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ سَرِيعُ ٱلۡحِسَابِ ١٩\nThe reason for unity and harmony is adhering to all religious teachings which is the worship of Allah alone, both inwardly and outwardly as He ordained. The end result for that is receiving Allah's mercy and pleasure, happiness in this life and the Hereafter, and shining of their faces. The reason for division is neglecting a portion of what was enjoined upon them, and the envy among themselves. The end result for that is Allah's punishment and curse, darkening of their faces and the disownment of the Messenger (r). Ibn Taimyah: 2/55.\nFor Muslim nation, what is the reason for unity and harmony? What is the reason for division?\nوَمَا ٱخۡتَلَفَ ٱلَّذِينَ أُوتُواْ ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ إِلَّا مِنۢ بَعۡدِ مَا جَآءَهُمُ ٱلۡعِلۡمُ بَغۡيَۢا بَيۡنَهُمۡۗ وَمَن يَكۡفُرۡ بِايَٰتِ ٱللَّهِ فَإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ سَرِيعُ ٱلۡحِسَابِ ١٩\nThey disputed after becoming aware of the truth due to envy. Ibn Juzay: 1/139.\nThe verse identifies a reason for their dispute. What is it?\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ يَكۡفُرُونَ بِٔاَيَٰتِ ٱللَّهِ وَيَقۡتُلُونَ ٱلنَّبِيِّۧنَ بِغَيۡرِ حَقّٖ وَيَقۡتُلُونَ ٱلَّذِينَ يَأۡمُرُونَ بِٱلۡقِسۡطِ مِنَ ٱلنَّاسِ فَبَشِّرۡهُم بِعَذَابٍ أَلِيمٍ ٢١\nThis verse indicates that enjoining good and forbidding evil was obligatory in earlier nations. Al-Qurtubi: 5/73.\nExplain the importance of enjoining good and forbidding evil.\nwords\nوَالقَانِتِينَThe obedient to Allah\nقَائِمًا بِالقِسطِAllah is the Upholder of justice in all matters\nبَغيًاEnvy and transgression\nحَبِطَتTheir deeds have become worthless"],[53,"§Al-Imran, Al-Waqi'ah\ndeeds\nAsk Allah to direct you to doing good deeds, for all good is in His Hand, and He dispenses it through the hands of whomever He wills of His servants.\nWrite a message in which you warn against taking the disbelievers as allies, and caution those who are deceived by them.\nSupplicate Allah to grant you sincerity, for He Knows what is in your heart.\nguid\nIt is a grave sin for a believer who to be called upon to follow the Quran and Sunnah and then reject their rulings due to his own desires. May Allah protect us.\nThe physical and mental punishment in the Hellfire is immense.\nFabricating lies about religion, innovating religious practices, and speaking about it without knowledge are among the most corrupting things to religion and belief.\nProvision is in the hands of Allah alone, others are only means that Allah has determined to deliver this provision, so if you ask, then ask Allah.\nrefl\nأَلَمۡ تَرَ إِلَى ٱلَّذِينَ أُوتُواْ نَصِيبٗا مِّنَ ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ يُدۡعَوۡنَ إِلَىٰ كِتَٰبِ ٱللَّهِ لِيَحۡكُمَ بَيۡنَهُمۡ ثُمَّ يَتَوَلَّىٰ فَرِيقٞ مِّنۡهُمۡ وَهُم مُّعۡرِضُونَ ٢٣\nWhoever turns away from the truth while he is fully aware of it, Allah will take away his knowledge as if he were never aware of it. Al-Alusi: 3/50.\nWhat is the significance of describing those who were given the Scripture as turning away in aversion?\nذَٰلِكَ بِأَنَّهُمۡ قَالُواْ لَن تَمَسَّنَا ٱلنَّارُ إِلَّآ أَيَّامٗا مَّعۡدُودَٰتٖۖ وَغَرَّهُمۡ فِي دِينِهِم مَّا كَانُواْ يَفۡتَرُونَ ٢٤\nTheir indifference toward following the truth because of their belief that they will be safe from Allah's punishment emboldened them to commit such a disregard. Ibn Ashur: 3/211.\nWhat is the consequence of the arrogant believing that Hellfire will only touch them for a few days?\nوَتُخۡرِجُ ٱلۡحَيَّ مِنَ ٱلۡمَيِّتِ وَتُخۡرِجُ ٱلۡمَيِّتَ مِنَ ٱلۡحَيِّۖ\nThis is the greatest evidence of Allah's power, and that all things are subjugated and controlled, and they do not possess any control over anything. The fact that Allah creates opposites, and creates some things from their opposites indicates that all things are subjugated. Al-Saadi: 127.\nHow does the verse indicate the perfection of Allah's power and the weakness of the creatures?\nلَّا يَتَّخِذِ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنُونَ ٱلۡكَٰفِرِينَ أَوۡلِيَآءَ مِن دُونِ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَۖ وَمَن يَفۡعَلۡ ذَٰلِكَ فَلَيۡسَ مِنَ ٱللَّهِ فِي شَيۡءٍ إِلَّآ أَن تَتَّقُواْ مِنۡهُمۡ تُقَىٰةٗۗ\nIt is confirmed that anything that is conventionally highly regarded and considered by Muslims as alliance with the disbelievers is indeed forbidden, particularly when weak Muslims are affected by it. Al-Alusi: 3/120.\nWhat is the type of alliance with disbelievers that is forbidden?\nقُلۡ إِن تُخۡفُواْ مَا فِي صُدُورِكُمۡ أَوۡ تُبۡدُوهُ يَعۡلَمۡهُ ٱللَّهُۗ وَيَعۡلَمُ مَا فِي ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَمَا فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِۗ وَٱللَّهُ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَيۡءٖ قَدِيرٞ ٢٩\nThis is a threat from Allah that He is all-Knowing and Most Capable of punishing them. A threat cannot be fulfilled if one of these two things is present: Ignorance of the criminal's crime, or inability to punish him. Therefore, when Allah informed them of his comprehensive knowledge and omnipotence, they knew that He would not let them escape his punishment. Ibn Ashur: 3/222.\nIn this verse, Allah combines His knowledge and capability. Why?\nقُلۡ إِن تُخۡفُواْ مَا فِي صُدُورِكُمۡ أَوۡ تُبۡدُوهُ يَعۡلَمۡهُ ٱللَّهُۗ وَيَعۡلَمُ مَا فِي ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَمَا فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِۗ وَٱللَّهُ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَيۡءٖ قَدِيرٞ ٢٩\nThis is a warning from Allah to His servants that they do not commit what He has forbidden and disliked, for He knows all their affairs, and is able to hasten their punishment. When He gives respite to some of them, He delays their punishment, but He is swift and Mighty in taking account. Ibn Kathir: 1/338.\nWhat does a Muslim gain from being aware of Allah's unlimited knowledge and capability?\nقُلۡ إِن تُخۡفُواْ مَا فِي صُدُورِكُمۡ أَوۡ تُبۡدُوهُ يَعۡلَمۡهُ ٱللَّهُۗ وَيَعۡلَمُ مَا فِي ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَمَا فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِۗ وَٱللَّهُ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَيۡءٖ قَدِيرٞ ٢٩\nThis contains guidance for purifying hearts and being mindful of Allah's knowledge at all times, so that the servant will be ashamed before his Lord to see his heart as a place for every bad thought. Rather, he should occupy his thoughts with what brings him closer to Allah, such as contemplating a verse from the Quran or a Hadith of the Messenger of Allah, or thinking and researching knowledge that may benefit him, contemplating the creation and blessings of Allah, or offering sincere advice to Allah's servants. Al-Saadi: 128.\nWhat should be your attitude when you know that Allah is aware of what is in your heart at all times?\nwords\nتُولِجُYou bring about\nتَتَّقُوا مِنهُم تُقَاةًTaking precaution against them in prudence"],[54,"§Al-Imran\ndeeds\nDo a good deed today such as feeding the hungry, helping the needy, or any other good deed, and you will find it present before your eyes on the Last Day.\nSearch in the Quran for three reasons to be loved by Allah, then strive to implement them to attain Allah's love.\nAsk for refuge with Allah for yourself, your offspring and family from satan.\nguid\nKeep away from doing evil or being in evil places before you wish for that on the Last Day but are unable to do so.\nFollowing the authentic Sunnah of the Messenger (r) is the only way to attain Allah's Love.\nNaturally, a male is different from a female, therefore, the responsibilities and burdens assigned to the male are in harmony with the nature of his creation, and the same is true for the female.\nrefl\nوَيُحَذِّرُكُمُ ٱللَّهُ نَفۡسَهُۥۗ وَٱللَّهُ رَءُوفُۢ بِٱلۡعِبَادِ ٣٠\nAllah, the Almighty, will take vengeance on those who transgress and forget that they are slaves of Him. Al-Biqai: 2/61.\nWhat is inferred from this verse: (And Allah warns you of Himself)?\nوَيُحَذِّرُكُمُ ٱللَّهُ نَفۡسَهُۥۗ\nAllah reiterates the admonition to fear Him, out of kindness and mercy toward us, lest our hearts become hard with the passage of time. This is a combination between encouragement that leads to hope and righteous deeds and warnings that lead to fear of Allah and abandoning sins. Al-Saadi: 128.\nIn this verse, Allah reiterates the admonition to fear Him. Why?\nقُلۡ إِن كُنتُمۡ تُحِبُّونَ ٱللَّهَ فَٱتَّبِعُونِي يُحۡبِبۡكُمُ ٱللَّهُ\nThis noble verse is a ruling on those who claim to love Allah, yet they do not follow the way of Muhammad (r). Such people are not true in their claim until they follow the Sharia of Muhammad (r) and his religion in their words and actions. Ibn Kathir: 1/338.\nThis verse indicates the importance of verifying the authenticity of the Hadiths of the Prophet. Explain.\nقُلۡ إِن كُنتُمۡ تُحِبُّونَ ٱللَّهَ فَٱتَّبِعُونِي يُحۡبِبۡكُمُ ٱللَّهُ وَيَغۡفِرۡ لَكُمۡ ذُنُوبَكُمۡۚ وَٱللَّهُ غَفُورٞ رَّحِيمٞ ٣١\nThis is because the Messenger is the one who calls to all things loved by Allah, and everything loved by Allah is enjoined by the Messenger (r); therefore, Allah's love and the messenger's call are inseparable. Ibn Taimyah: 2/60.\nWhy is following the Messenger (r) a sign of being loved by Allah?\nقُلۡ أَطِيعُواْ ٱللَّهَ وَٱلرَّسُولَۖ فَإِن تَوَلَّوۡاْ فَإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَا يُحِبُّ ٱلۡكَٰفِرِينَ ٣٢\nThis indicates that opposing the Messenger's way is disbelief. Indeed, Allah does not love anyone who is described as such, even if he claims that he loves Allah and seeks to draw closer to Him, until he follows the unlettered Prophet, the final Messenger (r). Ibn Kathir: 1/338.\nThere is a big risk in opposing the Messenger's (r) way. Explain.\nوَلَيۡسَ ٱلذَّكَرُ كَٱلۡأُنثَىٰۖ وَإِنِّي سَمَّيۡتُهَا مَرۡيَمَ\nIt indicates that the male is made to exceed the female, that naming of the child is required at the time of birth, and that the mother may name the child if the father does not object. Al-Saadi: 129.\nList some beneficial points from this verse?\nكُلَّمَا دَخَلَ عَلَيۡهَا زَكَرِيَّا ٱلۡمِحۡرَابَ وَجَدَ عِندَهَا رِزۡقٗاۖ قَالَ يَٰمَرۡيَمُ أَنَّىٰ لَكِ هَٰذَاۖ قَالَتۡ هُوَ مِنۡ عِندِ ٱللَّهِۖ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ يَرۡزُقُ مَن يَشَآءُ بِغَيۡرِ حِسَابٍ ٣٧\nIt indicates that this provision from Allah is a continuous and immeasurable gift. It is a provision that cannot be tracked, and the greatest gratitude for the provision of Allah is for the servant to acknowledge that it is from Him. Al-Biqai: 2/75.\nWhat the greatest gratitude for the provision of Allah?\nwords\nنَذَرتُ لکI have vowed to You\nمُحَرَّرًاDedicated for Your services\nأُعِيذُهَاI seek refuge with you for her\nالرَّجِيمِExpelled from the mercy of Allah\nالمِحرَابَPrayer chamber"],[55,"§Al-Imran\ndeeds\nSupplicate Allah today by saying\nMaintain your daily Athkar (Remembrance of Allah) in the morning, evening and after the obligatory prayers.\nGlorify Allah often today and throughout all of your affairs.\nguid\nWhen you see a blessing from Allah upon someone, then ask Allah for whatever you want. When Zachariah saw Allah's blessing upon Mary, he asked Him for a child, and his prayer was answered.\nChoose nice names with good meanings for your children, and keep away from strange and unusual names.\nWhen Allah chooses someone for a noble task, he should turn to Allah in gratitude, seek His Help to fulfill the task while maintaining patience in carrying it out.\nrefl\nهُنَالِكَ دَعَا زَكَرِيَّا رَبَّهُۥۖ قَالَ رَبِّ هَبۡ لِي مِن لَّدُنكَ ذُرِّيَّةٗ طَيِّبَةًۖ إِنَّكَ سَمِيعُ ٱلدُّعَآءِ ٣٨\nIn his request, Zachariah (u) used the word (grant me), which is giving with nothing in return. This is quite suitable in this case since both Zachariah (u) and his wife were incapable of contributing to the coming of their child; he was old and she was barren unable to bear children. Al-Alusi: 3/144.\nIn his request, Zachariah used the word (grant me). Why?\nفَنَادَتۡهُ ٱلۡمَلَٰٓئِكَةُ وَهُوَ قَآئِمٞ يُصَلِّي فِي ٱلۡمِحۡرَابِ أَنَّ ٱللَّهَ يُبَشِّرُكَ بِيَحۡيَىٰ\nThe scholars differed as to why he was named \"Yahia,\" [Its Arabic meaning is one who lives]. Ibn Abbas (t) said: It is because Allah revived with him the barrenness of his mother. Qatadah said: It is because Allah revives his heart with faith. It was also said that he was named \"Yahia\" because he was martyred, and martyrs are alive. Al-Baghawi: 1/348.\nAllah named the child of Zachariah \"Yahia\". Why?\nءَايَتُكَ أَلَّا تُكَلِّمَ ٱلنَّاسَ ثَلَٰثَةَ أَيَّامٍ إِلَّا رَمۡزٗاۗ\n(O my Lord! Give me a sign) Meaning: A sign that this child will come. He said: (Your sign is that you will not speak to people for three days except by gestures), that is: Your tongue will be prevented from speaking to them, without suffering any physical harm, so you will only be able to communicate by means of gestures, and this is a great sign that you cannot speak. There is an amazing contrast: Just as Allah may prevent causes from leading to effects even when they are present, He may also make things happen without the causes that would lead to them. This serves to demonstrate that all causes and means are subject to His will and decree. Al-Saadi: 130.\nThe inability of Zachariah (u) to speak and the birth of his child by his barren wife were two great signs from Allah. Explain.\nإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ ٱصۡطَفَىٰكِ\nAllah chose her for her extensive worship of Him, her asceticism, honor and purity from evil thoughts. Ibn Kathir: 1/342.\nWhy was Mary chosen by Allah?\nيَٰمَرۡيَمُ ٱقۡنُتِي لِرَبِّكِ وَٱسۡجُدِي وَٱرۡكَعِي مَعَ ٱلرَّٰكِعِينَ ٤٣\nBowing means humility and submissiveness to Allah, as if commanding her to do so would keep her from falling into the pitfalls of arrogance and haughtiness due to her high status. Al-Alusi: 3/157.\nWhy was Mary (o) commanded to prostrate and bow before Allah?\nيَٰمَرۡيَمُ ٱقۡنُتِي لِرَبِّكِ وَٱسۡجُدِي وَٱرۡكَعِي مَعَ ٱلرَّٰكِعِينَ ٤٣\nAfter informing her of her high status and her complete closeness to Allah, the angels commended Mary (o) to be mindful of the prayers, so that she would not slacken or neglect worship. Al-Alusi: 3/156.\nThe angels said to Mary: (Worship your Lord devoutly, and prostrate and bow with those who bow). What is inferred from that?\nوَٱسۡجُدِي وَٱرۡكَعِي مَعَ ٱلرَّٰكِعِينَ ٤٣\nProstration and bowing are singled out for mention because of their virtue and their indication of the ultimate submission to Allah. Al-Saadi: 130.\nWhy are prostration and bowing singled out for mention?\nwords\nلدنکFrom You\nوَحَصُورًاAbstinent from sins and lusts\nعَاقِرٌA barren woman\nرَمزًاBy gestures\nيُلقُونَ أَقلاَمَهُمCast lots with their pens"],[56,"§Al-Imran\ndeeds\nKnowledge is a grant and a gift from Allah, the greatest of which is knowledge of the Quran, so, ask Him, the Giver, to grant you useful knowledge.\nStudy and reflect considerably on the meanings of the verses of the Quran so that you may be granted wisdom.\nIdentify steps you can take to make friends who will help you obey Allah.\nguid\nAmong the motives of a preacher who invites others to Allah are:Compassion, kindness, and the desire for what is best for others.\nIt is wise for a preacher to have a group of supporters whom he teaches, so they carry out the burden of preaching others with him.\nAmong the signs of the allies of Allah are: Clarity in their way of life, their explicit declaration of their allegiance to the religion of Allah, the Almighty, and their support for the reformers.\nrefl\nقَالَتۡ رَبِّ أَنَّىٰ يَكُونُ لِي وَلَدٞ وَلَمۡ يَمۡسَسۡنِي بَشَرٞۖ\nIn His wisdom, Allah takes a gradual approach by informing His servants of what is strange as an introduction to that which is stranger. Hence, He first of all mentions the creation of Yahia (u), the son of Zakariya (u), who was born to parents, one of whom was elderly and the other was barren. Then He mentions something stranger and more amazing than that, which was the creation of Jesus (u) through a mother, without a father, in order to show His servants that He does what He wills, and that whatever He wills happens, and whatever He does not will not happen. Al-Saadi: 131.\nThe story of Yahia (u) precedes the story of Jesus (u). Why?\nقَالَتۡ رَبِّ أَنَّىٰ يَكُونُ لِي وَلَدٞ وَلَمۡ يَمۡسَسۡنِي بَشَرٞۖ قَالَ كَذَٰلِكِ ٱللَّهُ يَخۡلُقُ مَا يَشَآءُۚ إِذَا قَضَىٰٓ أَمۡرٗا فَإِنَّمَا يَقُولُ لَهُۥ كُن فَيَكُونُ ٤٧\nThe bringing of Jesus (u) into existence is expressed using the word (create) since it was done in a supernatural way. When a maker makes something using natural materials and applying normal process, he does not say: I created; rather he says: I made. Ibn Ashur: 3/249.\nThe verse uses the word (creates) instead of \"makes.\" Why\nوَأُبۡرِئُ ٱلۡأَكۡمَهَ وَٱلۡأَبۡرَصَ وَأُحۡيِ ٱلۡمَوۡتَىٰ بِإِذۡنِ ٱللَّهِۖ\nMany scholars said that Allah sent every Prophet with a miracle suitable to the people of his time. As for Jesus (u), he was sent during a time when medicine and natural sciences were advanced. Jesus brought them signs that no one can do unless he is supported by Allah. How could a physician bring inanimate objects back to life, or treat the blind and the leper, while resurrecting someone who is in his grave, bound until the Day of Judgment? Ibn Kathir: 2/37.\nIn His wisdom, Allah speaks to the people in terms of what they know. Explain this through the miracle of Jesus (u).\nوَأُبۡرِئُ ٱلۡأَكۡمَهَ وَٱلۡأَبۡرَصَ\nThese two disabilities are singled out due to their incurable nature. Since medicine was predominant during the time of Jesus (u), he showed them a miracle that they can truly appreciate. Al-Baghawi: 1/354.\nWhy was Jesus (u) given this miracle?\nوَلِأُحِلَّ لَكُم بَعۡضَ ٱلَّذِي حُرِّمَ عَلَيۡكُمۡۚ\nJewish law had many restrictions and that is why Jesus (u) said: (And to make lawful for you some of what was forbidden to you). Ibn Taimyah: 2/69.\nJewish law is characterized by a trait, what is it?\nوَلِأُحِلَّ لَكُم بَعۡضَ ٱلَّذِي حُرِّمَ عَلَيۡكُمۡۚ وَجِئۡتُكُم بِٔاَيَةٖ مِّن رَّبِّكُمۡ فَٱتَّقُواْ ٱللَّهَ وَأَطِيعُونِ ٥٠\n(So fear Allah and obey me), politeness toward the Benefactor [Allah] is more important, and fear of Him is more just and obligatory, lest He cut off his benevolence and cease His favors. Al-Biqai: 2/94.\nThe benevolence of Allah is mentioned before commanding to fear Him. Why?\nإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ رَبِّي وَرَبُّكُمۡ فَٱعۡبُدُوهُۚ هَٰذَا صِرَٰطٞ مُّسۡتَقِيمٞ ٥١\nMeaning: I do not call you to do something unless I do it before you. I never claim to be a god nor do I call to worship anything but Allah, the Almighty, as the Antichrist (Ad-Dajjal) and other liars claim, where supernatural phenomena appear at their hands as a test from Allah to His servants, and they use these miracles to seek glory in the land and superiority over people. Al-Biqai: 2/94.\nWhy does the term (my Lord) precede the term (your Lord)?\nwords\nالأَكمَهَOne who is born blind\nالحَوَارِيُّونَThe disciples of Jesus (peace be upon him)"],[57,"§Al-Imran\ndeeds\nIdentify one of your needs, then look at an act of worship that you perform, and supplicate to Allah, the Almighty, through that act of worship.\nRead about the major signs of the Hour (Day of Judgment) from an authentic source of the Prophet's Hadiths.\nThink of an issue that is hard for you to understand, then search the Quran for verses which address that issue so that you may be guided to the truth.\nguid\nDo not be concerned about conspiracies and plots against Islam and Muslims, for Allah is the protector of His religion and His allies.\nBeware of being too deep in disobedience to Allah while His favors keep coming to you, for this could be progressively leading you to destruction. May Allah protect us all.\nBeware of quarreling and arguing without evidence, for you will be held accountable for it on the Last Day.\nrefl\nرَبَّنَآ ءَامَنَّا بِمَآ أَنزَلۡتَ وَٱتَّبَعۡنَا ٱلرَّسُولَ فَٱكۡتُبۡنَا مَعَ ٱلشَّٰهِدِينَ ٥٣\n(Among those who bear witness), count us among those nations who bear witness to the truth. It is also said that it means: Count us among the nation of Muhammad (r). Ibn Juzay: 1/147.\nWhat should you do to be included in this supplication?\nوَمَكَرُواْ وَمَكَرَ ٱللَّهُۖ وَٱللَّهُ خَيۡرُ ٱلۡمَٰكِرِينَ ٥٤\nAllah's plan is to lure them from where they do not know. Ibn Abbas (t) said: Every time they commit a sin, We renew for them a blessing.\" Al-Qurtubi: 5/151.\nIn this verse, a certain type of plan by Allah is mentioned. Explain.\nوَجَاعِلُ ٱلَّذِينَ ٱتَّبَعُوكَ فَوۡقَ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوٓاْ إِلَىٰ يَوۡمِ ٱلۡقِيَٰمَةِۖ\n(Above those who disbelieve) above them by having the conclusive proof and establishing evidence. It is also said that it is by glory and victory. Al-Qurtubi: 5/156.\nHow do the followers of Tawhīd become superior to others?\nوَجَاعِلُ ٱلَّذِينَ ٱتَّبَعُوكَ فَوۡقَ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوٓاْ إِلَىٰ يَوۡمِ ٱلۡقِيَٰمَةِۖ ثُمَّ إِلَيَّ مَرۡجِعُكُمۡ فَأَحۡكُمُ بَيۡنَكُمۡ فِيمَا كُنتُمۡ فِيهِ تَخۡتَلِفُونَ ٥٥\nThey are the believers from the nation of Muhammad (r) who believed in Jesus (u), and followed his call to the Oneness of Allah—they are above the disbelievers, prevailing over them with glory, strength, and proof. Al-Baghawi: 1/361.\nAllah Promised the followers of Jesus (u) victory and empowerment. Does this include the nation of Muhammad (r)? Explain.\nوَأَمَّا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ وَعَمِلُواْ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ فَيُوَفِّيهِمۡ أُجُورَهُمۡۗ\nThis indicates that they will be rewarded in this world for their good deeds, such as honor, glory, victory, and a good life, but the full rewards will be given on the Day of Resurrection, when they will find what they sent forth of good deeds rewarded abundantly. Hence, Allah will give each one who did good deeds the reward of his deeds, and give them more from His bounty and generosity. Al-Saadi: 132.\nIn this verse, the believers are rewarded in this life and the Hereafter. How?\nإِنَّ مَثَلَ عِيسَىٰ عِندَ ٱللَّهِ كَمَثَلِ ءَادَمَۖ خَلَقَهُۥ مِن تُرَابٖ ثُمَّ قَالَ لَهُۥ كُن فَيَكُونُ ٥٩\nThis verse is an argument against Christians who say: How can there be a son without a father? So, Allah likens him to Adam (u) whom He created without a mother or a father, which is even stranger than what they excluded, and is irrefutable evidence against their saying. Ibn Juzay: 1/147.\nThis verse contains irrefutable evidence against Christians saying. Explain briefly.\nٱلۡحَقُّ مِن رَّبِّكَ فَلَا تَكُن مِّنَ ٱلۡمُمۡتَرِينَ ٦٠\nThis verse and what comes after offer proof for an important principle, which is that where there is evidence that something is true and one is certain of it, whether it is an issue of belief or otherwise, he must be certain that everything that opposes it must be false, and any argument in support of that opposing view is flawed, whether one is able to see the flaw or not. His inability to refute that argument should not make him doubt what he knows, because whatever is contrary to the truth is false. Allah says: (And what is there apart from truth but error) [10:32]. Following this principle will help one deal with many specious arguments that may be presented by philosophers and logicians. If a person tries to highlight the flaws, that is good but is not necessary; otherwise, he should focus on his task, which is explaining the truth on the basis of evidence and calling people to it. Al-Saadi: 133.\nHow does a Muslim deal with the doubts raised about matters of faith whose meaning is clear and explicit from the Quran and Sunnah?\nwords\nمتوفیکI shall take you from earth\nنَبتَهِلInvoke the curse of Allah upon the liars among us"],[58,"§Al-Imran\ndeeds\nStart today by setting a program for yourself to read the stories of the Quran and collect the lessons and morals from them.\nEmail some disbelievers a translation of the meanings of this noble verse and its interpretation in their language.\nIn light of these verses, write an article on the etiquettes of good dialogue and share it with your colleagues.\nguid\nWhen you see the wide-spread corruption of misguided people, just remember that Allah is fully aware of it, and He will retribute them for it.\nThe Prophets of Allah are infallible in what they convey from Him. Whoever claims infallibility other than them, then indeed he is a liar, while some of his followers may elevate him to the status of god, Allah forbids.\nArgumentation should only be about what you know. As for things that you do not know, do not argue or dispute about them.\nrefl\nقُلۡ يَٰٓأَهۡلَ ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ تَعَالَوۡاْ إِلَىٰ كَلِمَةٖ سَوَآءِۢ بَيۡنَنَا وَبَيۡنَكُمۡ أَلَّا نَعۡبُدَ إِلَّا ٱللَّهَ وَلَا نُشۡرِكَ بِهِۦ شَيۡٔاً وَلَا يَتَّخِذَ بَعۡضُنَا بَعۡضًا أَرۡبَابٗا مِّن دُونِ ٱللَّهِۚ\nPerhaps the benefit of saying that to them -since you are the people of true knowledge- is establishing further proof against them, just as Allah referred to the testimony of the people of knowledge as proof against those who are stubborn. Al-Saadi: 134.\nWhat is the benefit in calling people of the Scripture to come to a word that is equitable?\nقُلۡ يَٰٓأَهۡلَ ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ تَعَالَوۡاْ إِلَىٰ كَلِمَةٖ سَوَآءِۢ بَيۡنَنَا وَبَيۡنَكُمۡ أَلَّا نَعۡبُدَ إِلَّا ٱللَّهَ وَلَا نُشۡرِكَ بِهِۦ شَيۡٔاً وَلَا يَتَّخِذَ بَعۡضُنَا بَعۡضًا أَرۡبَابٗا مِّن دُونِ ٱللَّهِۚ\nTawhīd (Oneness of Allah), although it is the origin of righteousness, is the greatest justice. Ibn Taimyah: 2/80.\nTawhīd is the greatest justice. Explain.\nوَلَا يَتَّخِذَ بَعۡضُنَا بَعۡضًا أَرۡبَابٗا مِّن دُونِ ٱللَّهِۚ فَإِن تَوَلَّوۡاْ فَقُولُواْ ٱشۡهَدُواْ بِأَنَّا مُسۡلِمُونَ ٦٤\nThis verse refutes the Shiat's claim that one must accept Imam's words without legal clarification, and that he makes lawful what Allah has made unlawful without proof from Sharia for doing that. Al-Qurtubi: 5/162.\nIn the light of this verse, how do you respond to the Shi'ites?\nهَٰٓأَنتُمۡ هَٰٓؤُلَآءِ حَٰجَجۡتُمۡ فِيمَا لَكُم بِهِۦ عِلۡمٞ فَلِمَ تُحَآجُّونَ فِيمَا لَيۡسَ لَكُم بِهِۦ عِلۡمٞۚ وَٱللَّهُ يَعۡلَمُ وَأَنتُمۡ لَا تَعۡلَمُونَ ٦٦\nThis verse proves that it is prohibited for one to argue about religious issues of which he has no knowledge and lacks the ability to verify his information. Al-Qurtubi: 5/165.\nWho has the right to debate and discuss religious issues?\nمَا كَانَ إِبۡرَٰهِيمُ يَهُودِيّٗا وَلَا نَصۡرَانِيّٗا وَلَٰكِن كَانَ حَنِيفٗا مُّسۡلِمٗا وَمَا كَانَ مِنَ ٱلۡمُشۡرِكِينَ ٦٧\nThese verses also encourage learning history, for it is a way to refute many false arguments and claims that are contrary to historical facts. Al-Saadi: 134.\nWhat is the importance of learning history for a student of religious studies?\nوَدَّت طَّآئِفَةٞ مِّنۡ أَهۡلِ ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ لَوۡ يُضِلُّونَكُمۡ وَمَا يُضِلُّونَ إِلَّآ أَنفُسَهُمۡ وَمَا يَشۡعُرُونَ ٦٩\nIt was said that the meaning of their misleading themselves is their insistence on misguidance due to what their souls have encouraged them to do despite their ability to follow guidance through clear arguments. Al-Alusi: 3/199.\nHow does a person mislead himself?\nوَدَّت طَّآئِفَةٞ مِّنۡ أَهۡلِ ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ لَوۡ يُضِلُّونَكُمۡ\nIt is well known whoever wishes for something, will strive to achieve his goal. This faction strives and exert all its effort to turn away the believers by casting doubts on their faith in every way they can. Al-Saadi: 134.\nWhat do the People of the Scripture wish for Muslims?\nwords\nكَلِمَةٍ سَوَاءٍA word that is equitable and true to adhere to\nحَنِيفًاOne who is inclining away from associating partners with Allah"],[59,"§Al-Imran\ndeeds\nAsk Allah from His bounty and mercy, for His bounty is beyond your comprehension.\nDebate an opponent and acknowledge the right points in his opinion to train yourself to be fair and speak the truth.\nRemember a trust that you are keeping for others and hasten to return it.\nguid\nEffecting the truth and acknowledging factual points in your opponent's statements is an Islamic method of fairness to others.\nArrogance and contempt for others are among the reasons for consuming people's wealth unjustly.\nDo not use your oath and swearing by Allah as a means for selling and profiting.\nrefl\nيَٰٓأَهۡلَ ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ لِمَ تَلۡبِسُونَ ٱلۡحَقَّ بِٱلۡبَٰطِلِ وَتَكۡتُمُونَ ٱلۡحَقَّ وَأَنتُمۡ تَعۡلَمُونَ ٧١\nIf the scholars mix truth with falsehood, and do not distinguish between them, but rather leave matters ambiguous, and conceal the truth which they are enjoined to make manifest, that results in concealment of the truth and the prevalence of falsehood. Hence, the common folk who are seeking the truth and want to know and follow it, will not be guided. What is required from the people of knowledge is to make the truth clear to the people, proclaim it openly, and distinguish truth from falsehood. Al-Saadi: 134-135.\nWhat are the ramifications when a scholar mixes truth with falsehood, and conceals truth from people in religious matters?\nوَلَا تُؤۡمِنُوٓاْ إِلَّا لِمَن تَبِعَ دِينَكُمۡ قُلۡ إِنَّ ٱلۡهُدَىٰ هُدَى ٱللَّهِ أَن يُؤۡتَىٰٓ أَحَدٞ مِّثۡلَ مَآ أُوتِيتُمۡ أَوۡ يُحَآجُّوكُمۡ عِندَ رَبِّكُمۡۗ قُلۡ إِنَّ ٱلۡفَضۡلَ بِيَدِ ٱللَّهِ يُؤۡتِيهِ مَن يَشَآءُۗ وَٱللَّهُ وَٰسِعٌ عَلِيمٞ ٧٣\nIn In essence, they say: Do not disclose, except to your followers, the knowledge that others [Muslims] were given similar to what you have been given; they were given a Book like the Torah, and a Prophet like Moses (u), and that they can argue against you and win on the Last Day. In short, they forbade each other from exposing these two facts lest Muslims become firm on their position, and Arab polytheists accept Islam. Al-Alusi: 3/200.\nJealousy and envy prevent one from accepting the truth. Explain in light of this verse.\nوَمِنۡ أَهۡلِ ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ مَنۡ إِن تَأۡمَنۡهُ بِقِنطَارٖ يُؤَدِّهِۦٓ إِلَيۡكَ وَمِنۡهُم مَّنۡ إِن تَأۡمَنۡهُ بِدِينَارٖ لَّا يُؤَدِّهِۦٓ إِلَيۡكَ إِلَّا مَا دُمۡتَ عَلَيۡهِ قَآئِمٗاۗ\nThis verse indicates that the people of the Scripture are divided into two categories: Trustworthy and deceitful. The use of the expression (a great amount) indicates that whoever returns it back, will definitely return back what is less. Ibn Juzay: 1/150.\nThe Holy Quran is fair with its opponents of different faiths. Explain.\nوَمِنۡ أَهۡلِ ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ مَنۡ إِن تَأۡمَنۡهُ بِقِنطَارٖ يُؤَدِّهِۦٓ إِلَيۡكَ وَمِنۡهُم مَّنۡ إِن تَأۡمَنۡهُ بِدِينَارٖ لَّا يُؤَدِّهِۦٓ إِلَيۡكَ إِلَّا مَا دُمۡتَ عَلَيۡهِ قَآئِمٗاۗ\nTrust is of immense importance in Islamic Sharia. Its importance will show on the Last Day when trust and kinship will stand on the right and left of the Sirat [the bridge on top of Hellfire], as it is stated in Sahih Muslim, and only those who maintained them will be able to cross. Al-Qurtubi: 5/178-179.\nIn brief, describe the importance of trust, and the risk of breaking the trust.\nذَٰلِكَ بِأَنَّهُمۡ قَالُواْ لَيۡسَ عَلَيۡنَا فِي ٱلۡأُمِّيِّۧنَ سَبِيلٞ وَيَقُولُونَ عَلَى ٱللَّهِ ٱلۡكَذِبَ\n(We are under no obligation towards the gentiles), meaning: There is no sin on them for not paying them their money back because, on the basis of their corrupt claim and false opinions, they looked down on them and felt greatly superior to them, when in fact they [the Jews] were the lowest and most despised. They gave no sanctity to the gentiles (unlettered) with believing it to be permissible, thus, they combined the consumption of unlawful wealth with the belief that it was permissible, and this was fabricating lies about Allah. Al-Saadi: 135.\nThe Jews' control of most of the world's wealth is based on a corrupt foundation. Explain this from the verse.\nذَٰلِكَ بِأَنَّهُمۡ قَالُواْ لَيۡسَ عَلَيۡنَا فِي ٱلۡأُمِّيِّۧنَ سَبِيلٞ وَيَقُولُونَ عَلَى ٱللَّهِ ٱلۡكَذِبَ وَهُمۡ يَعۡلَمُونَ ٧٥\nThis is because the Jews said: The wealth of Arabs is a lawful gain for us because they do not follow our religion and have no sanctity, according to our Book. They consider it lawful to oppress others who are non-Jewish. Al-Baghawi: 1/371.\nTo what limit did the injustice and racism of the Jews reach?\nبَلَىٰۚ مَنۡ أَوۡفَىٰ بِعَهۡدِهِۦ وَٱتَّقَىٰ فَإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ يُحِبُّ ٱلۡمُتَّقِينَ ٧٦\nFulfilling covenants is an act of righteousness that Allah loves. Fulfilling covenants is enjoined in general, where it is considered a duty to do so by either the Islamic Sharia or by contractual terms. In all cases, this duty is commanded for the fulfilment of the covenant of Allah and that of the people. Ibn Taimyah: 2/85.\nWhat the virtue of fulfilling the covenants mentioned in the verse?\nwords\nتَلبِسُونَMix\nوَجهَ النَّهَارِThe beginning of the day\nبِقِنطَارٍA great amount of wealth\nالأُمِّيِّينَUnlettered people (Arabs)\nخَلاَقَA share"],[60,"§Al-Imran\ndeeds\nTeach someone, around you, the proper way of performing ablution and prayer. It is an example of teaching people progressively.\nIdentify a subject that you have learned, and put it into practice to follow the example of wise scholars.\nContribute to a project that supports the religion of Allah.\nguid\nSpreading lies about Allah and people is a sign of the audacity of the Jews.\nThe preacher and student of knowledge must always remember that he is calling others to Allah, not to himself.\nA scholar and a preacher should teach knowledge gradually to the people, and practice what he knows.\nrefl\nوَإِنَّ مِنۡهُمۡ لَفَرِيقٗا يَلۡوُۥنَ أَلۡسِنَتَهُم بِٱلۡكِتَٰبِ لِتَحۡسَبُوهُ مِنَ ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ وَمَا هُوَ مِنَ ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ وَيَقُولُونَ هُوَ مِنۡ عِندِ ٱللَّهِ وَمَا هُوَ مِنۡ عِندِ ٱللَّهِ\nWhat should be done is to preserve the words of the Scripture as they are and not change them, to understand their meanings properly and help others to do likewise. But these people did the opposite of that, and they gave an impression of incorrect meanings of the Scripture, either implicitly or explicitly. Al-Saadi: 136.\nThis verse identified a type of distortion to the Scripture. Explain.\nوَإِنَّ مِنۡهُمۡ لَفَرِيقٗا يَلۡوُۥنَ أَلۡسِنَتَهُم بِٱلۡكِتَٰبِ لِتَحۡسَبُوهُ مِنَ ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ وَمَا هُوَ مِنَ ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ وَيَقُولُونَ هُوَ مِنۡ عِندِ ٱللَّهِ وَمَا هُوَ مِنۡ عِندِ ٱللَّهِ وَيَقُولُونَ عَلَى ٱللَّهِ ٱلۡكَذِبَ وَهُمۡ يَعۡلَمُونَ ٧٨\nIn this verse, the present tense is used for these actions: (Alter) and (Say), to show that it is a continuing action that has become a habit for them. Ibn Ashur: 3/292.\nThe present tense is used to express their actions in the verse. Why?\nوَإِنَّ مِنۡهُمۡ لَفَرِيقٗا يَلۡوُۥنَ أَلۡسِنَتَهُم بِٱلۡكِتَٰبِ لِتَحۡسَبُوهُ مِنَ ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ وَمَا هُوَ مِنَ ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ\nAlteration was defined as: Distorting the words and distorting the meaning. Distorting the meaning is very common, and it had occurred even in this nation (Muslims) by some deviated groups. As for distorting the words, it had also occurred with many people who alter the words of Hadiths of the Prophet (r), and use inadmissible narrations. Ibn Taimyah: 2/86.\nAlteration of the revelation can be done in two ways. What are they?\nوَلَٰكِن كُونُواْ رَبَّٰنِيِّۧنَ بِمَا كُنتُمۡ تُعَلِّمُونَ ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ وَبِمَا كُنتُمۡ تَدۡرُسُونَ ٧٩\nWise scholars are ones who follow the path of Allah, affiliated with Him through perfect knowledge and deeds. The wise scholar is extremely devoted to Allah's religion and His obedience. Al-Biqai: 2/118.\nWhat are the traits of wise scholars?\nوَلَٰكِن كُونُواْ رَبَّٰنِيِّۧنَ بِمَا كُنتُمۡ تُعَلِّمُونَ ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ وَبِمَا كُنتُمۡ تَدۡرُسُونَ ٧٩\n(Wise scholars): Saeed bin Jubair said: A wise scholar is one who practices what he preaches. It was also said that wise scholars are at a higher level than rabbis who are scholars; however, wise scholars combine knowledge and insight for leading people. Al-Baghawi: 1/357.\nHow does one become a wise scholar?\nوَلَٰكِن كُونُواْ رَبَّٰنِيِّۧنَ بِمَا كُنتُمۡ تُعَلِّمُونَ ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ وَبِمَا كُنتُمۡ تَدۡرُسُونَ ٧٩\nThe benefit of study is knowledge, and the benefit of knowledge is putting it into practice, which is urge to do good deeds and being conscious of Allah. Al-Biqai: 2/118.\nWhat are the benefits of studying and seeking knowledge?\nوَإِذۡ أَخَذَ ٱللَّهُ مِيثَٰقَ ٱلنَّبِيِّۧنَ لَمَآ ءَاتَيۡتُكُم مِّن كِتَٰبٖ وَحِكۡمَةٖ ثُمَّ جَآءَكُمۡ رَسُولٞ مُّصَدِّقٞ لِّمَا مَعَكُمۡ لَتُؤۡمِنُنَّ بِهِۦ وَلَتَنصُرُنَّهُۥۚ قَالَ ءَأَقۡرَرۡتُمۡ وَأَخَذۡتُمۡ عَلَىٰ ذَٰلِكُمۡ إِصۡرِيۖ قَالُوٓاْ أَقۡرَرۡنَاۚ قَالَ فَٱشۡهَدُواْ وَأَنَا۠ مَعَكُم مِّنَ ٱلشَّٰهِدِينَ ٨١\nIt was narrated that Ali bin Abi Talib and Ibn Abbas and others have said: Not a Messenger sent by Allah since the time of Noah (u) except that he took a covenant with Allah that if Prophet Muhammad (r) is sent while he is still alive, then he must believe and support him. Moreover, he was also commanded by Allah to take the same covenant of his people to do the same. Ibn Taimyah: 2/88.\nExplain the high status of Prophet Muhammad (r).\nwords\nيَلوُونَAlter the Scripture\nرَبَّانِيِّينWise scholars\nإِصرِيMy covenant"],[61,"§Al-Imran\ndeeds\nInvite a disbeliever to Islam using modern means of communication, or other methods.\nIn light of this verse, share a message in which you refute the claim that all religions are the same.\nRecall a sin that you had committed and ask often for Allah's forgiveness, then give to charity so that Allah may pardon you.\nguid\nAn explicit rule that is not subject to interpretation or distortion: Islam is the only religion that Allah accepts from His servant.\nThe gate of repentance is never closed to a sinner, no matter how far he goes into disbelief or sins.\nThe best repentance is one that is followed by reform and calling others to Islam.\nrefl\nوَمَن يَبۡتَغِ غَيۡرَ ٱلۡإِسۡلَٰمِ دِينٗا فَلَن يُقۡبَلَ مِنۡهُ وَهُوَ فِي ٱلۡأٓخِرَةِ مِنَ ٱلۡخَٰسِرِينَ ٨٥\nThis verse nullifies all religions other than Islam. Ibn Juzay: 1/151.\nHow do you respond to one who claims that the followers of Judaism and Christianity are not disbelievers?\nوَمَن يَبۡتَغِ غَيۡرَ ٱلۡإِسۡلَٰمِ دِينٗا فَلَن يُقۡبَلَ مِنۡهُ وَهُوَ فِي ٱلۡأٓخِرَةِ مِنَ ٱلۡخَٰسِرِينَ ٨٥\nAllah makes clear that the religion that He is pleased with and accepts from His servants is Islam, and it will only be approved and accepted by Him when faith is combined with action. Ibn Taimyah: 2/96.\nWhen is religion accepted by Allah?\nكَيۡفَ يَهۡدِي ٱللَّهُ قَوۡمٗا كَفَرُواْ بَعۡدَ إِيمَٰنِهِمۡ وَشَهِدُوٓاْ أَنَّ ٱلرَّسُولَ حَقّٞ وَجَآءَهُمُ ٱلۡبَيِّنَٰتُۚ\nHence, these people will not be granted guidance, because the one who is expected to be guided is one who did not know the truth but is keen to seek it. Such person is deserving of being shown the path of guidance and being protected from misguidance by Allah. Al-Saadi: 137.\nWhat type of disbelievers from whom guidance and faith are expected?\nكَيۡفَ يَهۡدِي ٱللَّهُ قَوۡمٗا كَفَرُواْ بَعۡدَ إِيمَٰنِهِمۡ وَشَهِدُوٓاْ أَنَّ ٱلرَّسُولَ حَقّٞ وَجَآءَهُمُ ٱلۡبَيِّنَٰتُۚ\nMeaning: The proofs and evidence were established, testifying to the truth of what the Messenger brought them. The truth was thus explained to them, but they reverted to the darkness of polytheism. Therefore, how can such people deserve guidance after they willingly leapt into utter blindness. Al-Kathir: 1/359.\nWhy are those described in this verse unworthy of guidance?\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ بَعۡدَ إِيمَٰنِهِمۡ ثُمَّ ٱزۡدَادُواْ كُفۡرٗا لَّن تُقۡبَلَ تَوۡبَتُهُمۡ\nThey will not be helped to repent in any acceptable manner; rather Allah will prolong them to wander blindly in their transgression. Such people have barred themselves from taking measures of attaining their Lord's mercy, and they are the ones who blocked the way to repentance for themselves. Al-Saadi: 137.\nThe repentance of those described in this verse is not accepted. Why?\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ بَعۡدَ إِيمَٰنِهِمۡ ثُمَّ ٱزۡدَادُواْ كُفۡرٗا لَّن تُقۡبَلَ تَوۡبَتُهُمۡ وَأُوْلَٰٓئِكَ هُمُ ٱلضَّآلُّونَ ٩٠\nThat is because Allah has set a seal upon their hearts, hence they will not turn to Allah in sincere repentance that will endure and enable them to mend their ways. In another interpretation, there is no acceptance as they never repented because they exceeded those who are previously mentioned with their self-indulgence. Al-Biqai: 2/123.\nWhy is the repentance of one who repeatedly disbelieves after his faith not accepted?\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ وَمَاتُواْ وَهُمۡ كُفَّارٞ فَلَن يُقۡبَلَ مِنۡ أَحَدِهِم مِّلۡءُ ٱلۡأَرۡضِ ذَهَبٗا وَلَوِ ٱفۡتَدَىٰ بِهِۦٓۗ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ لَهُمۡ عَذَابٌ أَلِيمٞ وَمَا لَهُم مِّن نَّٰصِرِينَ ٩١\nAbu Omran said: I heard Anas bin Malik (t) narrating that the Prophet (r) said, \"Allah will say to the person with the least punishment in Hellfire on the Day of Resurrection: \"If you had everything on earth, would you ransom yourself?\" He will say: \"Yes.\" Then, Allah will say, \"I wanted something easier from you than this while you were in the backbone of Adam, that you not associate anything with Me, but you persisted in worshiping others besides Me.\" Al-Baghawi: 1/380.\nWhat will be said to the one with the least punishment in Hellfire on the Day of Resurrection?\nwords\nوَالأَسبَاطِThe Prophets of the Israelite twelve tribes"],[62,"§Al-Imran\ndeeds\nDetermine something you love and spend from it for the sake of Allah, so that you may attain the status of the righteous.\nSeek help from Allah, and supplicate Him often, then plan steps to overcome obstacles to reach the House of Allah in Makkah for Hajj or Umrah, for Allah is as His servant thinks of Him.\nAct differently from the Jews and Christians by letting your beard grow, trimming your moustache, and keeping your clothes above your ankles. Women should hide their adornment by wearing complete Hijab.\nguid\nOne will never attain righteousness until he spends in charity from his beloved wealth.\nAverting people from believing in Allah is indeed the work of the misguided and disbelievers.\nBeware of listening to the disbelievers in matters of religion and faith, as they will only bring you heedlessness and corruption.\nrefl\nلَن تَنَالُواْ ٱلۡبِرَّ حَتَّىٰ تُنفِقُواْ مِمَّا تُحِبُّونَۚ\nWhen one spends in charity from something he loves, it is considered much better in the sight of Allah than spending from another thing that he may not loves as much, even if both things are of the same value. Ibn Taimyah: 2/108.\nWhat is the best thing you spend from your wealth in charity that draws you nearer to Allah?\nكُلُّ ٱلطَّعَامِ كَانَ حِلّٗا لِّبَنِيٓ إِسۡرَٰٓءِيلَ إِلَّا مَا حَرَّمَ إِسۡرَٰٓءِيلُ عَلَىٰ نَفۡسِهِۦ مِن قَبۡلِ أَن تُنَزَّلَ ٱلتَّوۡرَىٰةُۚ قُلۡ فَأۡتُواْ بِٱلتَّوۡرَىٰةِ فَٱتۡلُوهَآ إِن كُنتُمۡ صَٰدِقِينَ ٩٣\nAz-Zajjaj said: This verse contains the greatest evidence of the Prophethood of our Prophet Muhammad (r), where he told the Jews that it was not in their Book ,and commanded them to bring the Torah but they refused to do so because they knew that what he said was a revelation from Allah. Al-Qurtubi: 5/204-205.\nThis verse contains evidence of the Prophethood of our Prophet Muhammad (r). What is it?\nإِنَّ أَوَّلَ بَيۡتٖ وُضِعَ لِلنَّاسِ لَلَّذِي بِبَكَّةَ مُبَارَكٗا وَهُدٗى لِّلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ٩٦\nBeing the first house of worship is the reason for preference, because houses of worship (mosques) are not differentiated in terms of worship, as they are equal in that regard. However, some take precedence due to the length of time of worship in them, the status of their builder, and the good intentions for their establishment. Ibn Ashur: 4/15.\nThe Ka'bah, the first house of worship, takes precedence over all mosques, Why?\nإِنَّ أَوَّلَ بَيۡتٖ وُضِعَ لِلنَّاسِ لَلَّذِي بِبَكَّةَ مُبَارَكٗا وَهُدٗى لِّلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ٩٦\n(Blessed), because the reward of worship in Makkah is greatly multiplied; or because anyone who performs Pilgrimage, circumambulate the Ka'bah, and keeps devotional retreat will be forgiven. Another reason of its blessing is what is mentioned in this verse, (A safe sanctuary to which are brought the fruits of all things) [28-57]. Moreover, it is said that its blessing is due to the continuity of worship around it. Al-Alusi: 4/5.\nList some of the blessings in the Sacred House (Ka'bah)?\nفِيهِ ءَايَٰتُۢ بَيِّنَٰتٞ مَّقَامُ إِبۡرَٰهِيمَۖ وَمَن دَخَلَهُۥ كَانَ ءَامِنٗاۗ\n(In it are clear signs), some of its clear signs are: A stone on which Abraham (u) stood, while raising the foundations of Ka'bah where the stone elevated him to reach the top of the Ka'bah. The higher the construction became, the higher the stone rose in the air until the construction was complete. Abraham's foot sank into the stone as if it were in mud, and that effect remains to this day. Birds avoid flying over the Ka'bah. The Ka'bah is protected by Allah from invading armies like when He destroyed the people of the elephant, and repelled tyrants away. The gushing of Zamzam water for Hagar, mother of Ishmael, by Gabriel’s nudge with his heel. Then, over a long time, the well of Zamzam became buried until Abdulmattalib (grandfather of Prophet Muhammad (r)) dug it again. Also, Zamzam water is beneficial for whatever it is drunk for, etc. Ibn Juzay: 1/153.\nList some of the signs of the sacred Ka'bah?\nوَلِلَّهِ عَلَى ٱلنَّاسِ حِجُّ ٱلۡبَيۡتِ مَنِ ٱسۡتَطَاعَ إِلَيۡهِ سَبِيلٗاۚ وَمَن كَفَرَ فَإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ غَنِيٌّ عَنِ ٱلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ٩٧\nWhoever is able to perform Pilgrimage and yet does not do so, while acknowledging the obligatory status of Pilgrimage, has disbelieved in the favors of Allah. If he denies its obligatory status, then he is an apostate. Al-Biqai: 2/128.\nLabeling one who did not perform Pilgrimage as a \"disbeliever.\" What is meant by that?\nوَلِلَّهِ عَلَى ٱلنَّاسِ حِجُّ ٱلۡبَيۡتِ\nThe actions and rulings of Allah, the Almighty, must have wisdom and benefit, and this is accepted. However, we do not accept that this benefit must be apparent to us, since the Wise One is not obliged to reveal His wisdom to the people. Al-Alusi: 4/11.\nIs there wisdom in all of Allah's commands for us? Is it necessary to know this wisdom?\nwords\nإِسرَائِيلَProphet Jacob (peace be upon him)\nبِبَكَّةَIn the holy city of Makkah\nمَقَامُ إِبرَاهِيمَA stone on which Abraham stood while erecting the Ka'bah"],[63,"§Al-Imran\ndeeds\nWrite a message about the benefits of unity and the harms of division.\nThank one of the people you know who is engaged in enjoining good and forbidding evil, and pray for him.\nBe keen today to enjoin what is right and forbid what is wrong so that you may be among the successful servants of Allah.\nguid\nReciting the Quran while reflecting on its meanings, studying the Prophet's Hadiths, and acting upon them are great reasons for steadfastness in faith.\nBeware of dying having changed and altered the religion of Allah Almighty, and say this supplication often: “O Controller of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion.\"\nA difference that is based on whims is evil for the individual and society.\nrefl\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ ٱتَّقُواْ ٱللَّهَ حَقَّ تُقَاتِهِۦ وَلَا تَمُوتُنَّ إِلَّا وَأَنتُم مُّسۡلِمُونَ ١٠٢\nThese righteous predecessors: Ibn Masoud, Alhasan, Ikrimah, Qatadah, and Muqatil all said in the meaning of this verse (as He should be feared): He is to be obeyed and not disobeyed, to be thanked and not denied, and to be remembered and not forgotten. Ibn Taimyah: 2/116.\nWhat is meant by fearing Allah, the Almighty, as He should be feared?\nوَلَا تَمُوتُنَّ إِلَّا وَأَنتُم مُّسۡلِمُونَ ١٠٢\nMeaning: Preserve your faith while you are well and safe, so that you die as Muslims. Allah, the Most Generous, has made it a habit of His generosity that whoever lives his life in a certain way, will surely die and be resurrected with the same. Ibn Kathir: 1/366.\nWhy is it important to adhere to the commands of Allah in this life?\nوَٱعۡتَصِمُواْ بِحَبۡلِ ٱللَّهِ جَمِيعٗا وَلَا تَفَرَّقُواْۚ\n(All together), do not let anyone of you deviate from it, and when you find someone who has deviated from it -even slightly- bring him back to it. Do not debate nor neglect nor overlook him, lest all things fall apart, and you would be frustrated. You will remain like one who securely ties a bundle of arrows with a rope, not letting a single one become separated from the others. Al-Biqai: 2/131.\nWhat is the significance of the word (all) in the command to hold fast?\nوَٱعۡتَصِمُواْ بِحَبۡلِ ٱللَّهِ جَمِيعٗا وَلَا تَفَرَّقُواْۚ\nThere is no evidence in this verse that it is forbidden to differ over minor issues since that is not a division. A division is what makes harmony and unity impossible. As for rulings on matters of jurisprudence, the disagreement regarding them is due to the deduction of precepts and the subtleties of the meanings of the Sharia. The Prophet's Companions continued to differ in the rulings on emerging issues, yet they were in complete harmony. Al-Qurtubi: 5/241.\nIs every difference in viewpoints considered a division and a rift?\nوَٱذۡكُرُواْ نِعۡمَتَ ٱللَّهِ عَلَيۡكُمۡ\nThis verse indicates that Allah loves for His servants to remember His blessings with their hearts and words, so that their gratitude and love for Him may increase, thus He would increase His bounty and blessings upon them. The greatest blessing of Allah that one may remember is the blessing of guidance to Islam. Al-Saadi: 142.\nHow does a believer remember his Lord's blessings? What is the benefit of this remembrance?\nوَلۡتَكُن مِّنكُمۡ أُمَّةٞ يَدۡعُونَ إِلَى ٱلۡخَيۡرِ وَيَأۡمُرُونَ بِٱلۡمَعۡرُوفِ وَيَنۡهَوۡنَ عَنِ ٱلۡمُنكَرِۚ وَأُوْلَٰٓئِكَ هُمُ ٱلۡمُفۡلِحُونَ ١٠٤\nPeople have different levels of responsibilities when it comes to changing evil and enjoining good: the scholars' duty is to alert the Rulers and Governors, and advise them of corrective actions. The duty of Rulers is changing evil with their power and authority. The duty of common people is protesting evil acts verbally and reporting them to the authority. This applies to acts of evil that can be permanent. If someone sees an obvious evil such as robbery, adultery, and the like, one should it change himself promptly in accordance with his capability. Ibn Atiyah: 1/486.\nPeople have different levels of responsibilities when it comes to enjoining good and forbidding evil. Explain.\nوَأَمَّا ٱلَّذِينَ ٱبۡيَضَّتۡ وُجُوهُهُمۡ فَفِي رَحۡمَةِ ٱللَّهِۖ هُمۡ فِيهَا خَٰلِدُونَ ١٠٧\nTheir faces will turn dark because of the disgrace, humiliation and shame in their hearts. The faces of the blessed will turn bright because of the joy, happiness, blessing and contentment in their hearts, the effects of which will appear on their faces. Al-Saadi: 341.\nMuslims' faces will turn bright while the disbelievers' faces will turn dark. Why?\nwords\nشَفَاThe edge"]])